ed on business development activity across all PUBSEC Government Agencies and Departments in Germany.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for an approachable and compelling communicator who loves working with public sector customers to uncover their needs and feels comfortable developing tailored value propositions around how Cohere’s platform can help them drive better mission and citizen outcomes. You’ll lay the foundation for Cohere’s growth by owning your territory and collaborating with teammates across Customer Success, Sales Development, Marketing, and Sales Engineering. You’ll be the voice of the field and help our Product and Engineering teams prioritize the Cohere roadmap with customer-centric care. In this highly self-directed role, you will thrive in a quickly evolving environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>As a Senior Account Executive, you will</strong>:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive net-new customer acquisition through targeted outbound activity, senior leader engagement, and relationship building in Germany.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and execute a sales plan for Germany, prioritizing accounts and opportunities through collaboration with Cohere leadership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a trusted advisor and thought partner to public sector customers and prospects by understanding their goals and shaping AI solutions that deliver measurable value</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with channel and regional partners, as well as major system integrators to scale outreach, accelerate adoption, and maximize customer success</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leverage senior-level relationships with executives and government decision-makers to drive strategic opportunities and long-term partnerships</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with Product and Engineering teams on strategic efforts to deliver enterprise and public-sector solutions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with SDRs and Marketing to drive top-of-funnel activity and overall territory growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the full sales cycle; including discovery, technical and business validation, proof-of-concept, procurement, and deal close within a team-selling environment</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You may be a good fit if you have:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">10+ years of direct public sector sales experience in Germany, with a proven track record of closing $3M+ annual quotas.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep knowledge of PUBSEC procurement and budget cycles, decision-making processes, and how to work with regional partners and resellers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Established network in Germany, including federal agencies, prime contractors, and industry associations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience selling SaaS, AI/ML, or enterprise software solutions to government clients.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High tolerance for ambiguity, you are both a strategist and a hands-on operator capable of building a market from the ground up</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong organizational skills, with the ability to manage multiple internal and external stakeholders across fast-moving deals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Creativity and strong technical acumen to structure unique, mutually beneficial partnerships</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication skills, you listen deeply, understand what matters to senior decision-makers, and confidently present to both technical and non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">English and German language proficiency essential.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Must be based in Germany with willingness to travel (25-35%).</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Full-Time Employees at Cohere enjoy these Perks:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A weekly lunch stipend of $75/£75 or equivalent in your local currency for lunch.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full health and dental benefits, including a separate budget for mental health.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">RRSP matching, 401K, Pension Scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">100% Parental Leave top-up for up to 6 months, for either parent.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Annual enrichment benefits:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Arts &amp; culture, fitness/wellness, quality time, and a workspace improvement credit.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Education &amp; learning stipend for conferences, courses, and coaching.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">6 weeks of paid vacation (30 working days!)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Budget for traveling to other offices if you are remote, plus an annual company offsite.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>How and Where We Work:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cohere is remote-friendly, but we also have offices in Toronto, London, New York City, San Francisco, Montreal, Paris, Berlin and Seoul with more opening soon.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">For those in the office: a daily lunch program, plenty of snacks, and regular community and social events.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">For those not near an office: a co-working benefit so you can work alongside others in your city.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everyone receives a $500 home office stipend to set up your workspace properly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">If any of the above doesn’t line up exactly with your experience, we still encourage you to apply. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />We strive to create an inclusive work environment for all; we welcome applicants from all backgrounds and are committed to providing equal opportunities. Should you require any accommodations during the recruitment process, please submit an<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/12a6IrLdF3kI2nonKSr4tiFuz18rLQbaeYV-JM9L4o9Q/edit"> Accommodations Request Form</a>, and we will work together to meet your needs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We may use AI-enabled tools to screen and assess applicants against the criteria for this position. This helps our recruiters identify potentially qualified candidates, but it doesn't limit the applications our recruiters may review or consider.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Beware of Scams: Cohere will never ask for payment or third-party services (e.g., CV writing) as part of our hiring process. All legitimate roles are listed on the Cohere careers page and LinkedIn only, with all communications from Cohere employees coming from an ----- or ----- email alias. If jobs are viewed on other sites then please verify these through our </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://cohere.com/careers"><em>official careers</em></a><em> page.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/cohere/senior-account-executive-germany-pubsec-berlin-germany-466760","tags":["Revenue"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1795740014},{"slug":"account-executive-dach-ai-supply-chain-saas-ae-munich-292368","company_name":"Luminovo GmbH","title":"Account Executive (DACH) | AI Supply Chain SaaS AE (d/f/m)","description":"<h1>About the role</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Electronics is a trillion-dollar industry that still runs on spreadsheets, email threads and part-search tabs. Luminovo is the AI platform that replaces them, and DACH is our home market, with 400+ customers worldwide.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're adding an Account Executive to our German-speaking team. You will sell our procurement intelligence platform to OEMs, from automotive suppliers to industrial equipment and medical device makers: procurement, supply chain and engineering leaders who want to cut component costs and see supply risk before it stops production. Our buyers rarely arrive knowing they have a problem worth solving, so you win through deep discovery, a sharp business case and trust built across several stakeholders.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will write the playbook with us. Our OEM motion in DACH is still being built, and you will shape how we sell to it, with a founder and a VP of Sales next to you.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1>Your performance objectives</h1><h2>Generate pipeline</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create qualified pipeline of roughly €420k–€500k ARR per quarter at Level 2 and €570k–€680k at Level 3, through your own outbound, events and the meetings our BDRs book, qualified with SPICED (Situation, Pain, Impact, Critical event, Decision criteria).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build your network: connect with 50+ relevant decision-makers at electronics manufacturers per quarter and represent Luminovo at 2–3 industry fairs a year.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ramp with clear targets: in your first 3 months, complete the discovery and demo certifications and all Lumiversity courses, and create 4 qualified opportunities at Level 2 or 6 at Level 3 (6 and 9 with BDR support). In your second quarter you work toward 50% of full quota, and from there toward full quota.</p></li></ul><h2>Close opportunities</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run demos tailored to each customer's pain and prove value with domain experts in workshops that quantify ROI: savings against market prices, risk exposure uncovered, disruptions avoided.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guide prospects through complex buyer journeys: map stakeholders, handle procurement and legal, close about €105k–€125k of new ARR per quarter at Level 2 or €143k–€169k at Level 3, and hand over smoothly to Customer Success.</p></li></ul><h2>Build your OEM playbook</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Within 6 months, document what works in the DACH OEM segment (messaging, discovery questions, objections) and contribute it to our sales playbook.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Feed customer and market insight to Product every month, with at least one concrete product input that lands on the roadmap.</p></li></ul><h2>Lead by example</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own your metrics (pipeline health, conversion, deal velocity) and use them to hit your quarterly targets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mentor our BDRs through call reviews and shared discovery, and ask for coaching after every major customer interaction.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1>Your potential growth path</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Months 1–6: master the product, close your first 5–10 deals, build your DACH network.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Months 6–18: take on larger deals and complex stakeholder setups, mentor BDRs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">18+ months: move into Enterprise AE (€100k+ deals), own strategic accounts, mentor junior AEs.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1>Your territory and work setup</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">German-speaking market (DACH) plus some English-speaking territories. Discovery, demos and negotiations happen in German and the company works in English, so you need both at a professional level. Hybrid at our Munich HQ or Berlin hub, with the sales team in the office three days a week. Occasional travel for retreats and industry events, costs covered.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1>Whom you'll be working with</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/cliftonlobo/">Clifton Lobo</a>, VP Global Sales, your manager, who coaches you on deal strategy and career progression</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/sebastian-schaal/">Sebastian Schaal</a>, co-founder, for positioning and pricing</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/inga-schwarz/">Inga Schwarz</a>, Team Lead and pioneer AE for OEM, your partner in building the OEM playbook</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/dasha-vyazemskaya/">Dasha</a> and our BDR team, who feed you qualified meetings</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/maxhungenbach/">Max Hungenbach</a> and RevOps for CRM, dashboards and enablement</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Marketing and Customer Success</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1>Why Luminovo</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Measurable product impact: our procurement intelligence shows OEMs where they pay above market and which parts put production at risk, so your business case starts from the customer's own BOMs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An open field: you shape the DACH OEM playbook with a founder and our VP Global Sales next to you</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI is part of how we work, from our MCP integrations to the agents our own teams build</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Psychological safety, honest feedback, an international and remote-first team</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Just so you know – we purposefully did not create a standard list of minimum qualifications for this role. We care much more about your motivation and ability to help us accelerate technical progress than we care just about your CV. If you're interested to find out more about why we banned requirements from our performance profiles – see <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/startup-grind/why-we-banned-requirements-from-our-job-descriptions-33a774e1a1c2">here</a>.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1></h1><h1><strong>⚡️ About Luminovo</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Luminovo is the first electronics supply chain platform that unites all data, processes, and stakeholders in the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://luminovo.com/resources/blog/a-short-primer-on-the-electronics-industry?utm_campaign=employer_branding&amp;utm_source=candidate-traffic">trillion-dollar electronics industry</a>.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We fundamentally believe that technology is the best tool that humankind has developed to tackle the biggest challenges we face as a society today. And we want to do our share in accelerating technological progress. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>We bring innovations to life faster and cheaper by creating a more connected and resilient electronics supply chain.</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To date, over 400 active customers worldwide are working with us towards this shared goal. Supported by leading investors such as Cherry Ventures, General Catalyst/LaFamiglia, Chalfen Ventures, and others, we have <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://luminovo.com/resources/blog/luminovo-raises-eu11-million-in-seed-funding-to-fix-the-broken-electronics-value-chain-with-transformative-software-suite">raised more than €20 million</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our core principles: putting people first &amp; building great things</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a remote-first company headquartered in Munich, our brilliant team is spread across cities including Munich, New York, Austin, Calgary, Berlin, London, Valencia, Nairobi, and Verona, among others. 🌍</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our team includes a mix of product enthusiasts, people advocates, business masterminds, and engineering experts. Among us are graduates from institutions like Stanford University and the University of Cambridge, as well as talented individuals with unconventional CVs. What matters most is their drive to build great things.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We provide an authentic environment based on psychological safety to empower Luminerds from various backgrounds to succeed, grow, and focus on impact. Putting people first means that we deeply care about who our employees are, what makes them unique, and what they excel at. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">See what employees and candidates have to say about Luminovo on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.kununu.com/de/luminovo">kununu</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.glassdoor.de/Bewertungen/luminovo-ai-Bewertungen-E2039308.htm">Glassdoor</a>.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><hr><p>Compensation: €86.5K – €143.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission • Multiple Ranges</p><ul><li>Germany | Level 2 • On-Target Earnings €86.5K – €115.3K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission</li><li>Germany | Level 3 • On-Target Earnings €132K – €143.5K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/luminovo-gmbh/account-executive-dach-ai-supply-chain-saas-ae-munich-292368","tags":["Revenue"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"🇩🇪 Munich (hybrid)","created_at":1795740014},{"slug":"business-development-representative-dach-ai-supply-chain-saas-bdr-munich-73470","company_name":"Luminovo GmbH","title":"Business Development Representative (DACH) | AI Supply Chain SaaS BDR (d/f/m)","description":"<h1>About the role</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Electronics is a trillion-dollar industry that still runs on spreadsheets, email threads and part-search tabs. Luminovo is the AI platform that replaces them, and DACH is our home market, with 400+ customers worldwide.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a BDR in our DACH team you are the engine behind our new pipeline. You find the procurement, supply chain and engineering leaders at electronics manufacturers who overpay for components or carry hidden supply risk, start the conversation, and hand our Account Executives meetings worth taking. We want you to build the outbound machine with us, not only run it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is the first step of a defined path: consistent target achievement gets you considered for promotion to a full-cycle Account Executive role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Your performance objectives</h1><h2>Generate pipeline</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and keep current a target list of OEM accounts in DACH (automotive suppliers, industrial equipment, medical devices), and map the decision-makers per account in engineering, procurement and supply chain, using Sales Navigator, Apollo and Clay.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run multichannel outbound (email, phone, LinkedIn, events) that books discovery calls for our AEs: 4 in month 1, 8 in month 2 and 12 per month from month 3 (16 per month at Level 3). Source your first qualified opportunities from month 2 and reach 6 per month by month 4 (8 at Level 3).</p></li></ul><h2>Qualify with precision</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run cold calls and discovery conversations in German that find the pain behind the title: the current process, the cost of delay, who decides. Hand over each meeting with clean notes so the AE never starts from zero.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Complete the discovery and demo certifications in your first weeks and all Lumiversity courses by the end of month 3, so every meeting you hand over meets our qualified-opportunity bar.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tell us fast which segments and messages convert.</p></li></ul><h2>Build an AI-powered outbound engine</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Within your first 90 days, design and ship one automation or agent that improves your own outbound (account research, personalized first lines, lead scoring), and show the result: reply rate, hours saved or meetings booked.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Share what works with the team, so the next BDR starts with your playbook.</p></li></ul><h2>Grow toward Account Executive</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learn the product and the electronics supply chain well enough to start co-running discovery calls with an AE.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own your numbers every week (activity, reply rate, meetings, acceptance) and bring market insights to sales, marketing and product.</p></li></ul><h1>Your potential growth path</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Months 1–3: master the product and our ICP, launch your first sequences, book your first qualified meetings.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Months 4–9: hit your meeting target consistently, ship your own automation, start co-running discovery with AEs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">After the ramp: consistent target achievement gets you considered for promotion to full-cycle Account Executive, following our sales progression framework.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Your territory and work setup</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">DACH market. Discovery calls and outreach happen in German and the company works in English, so you need both at a professional level. Hybrid in Munich or Berlin, with three office days per week. Occasional travel for team retreats and industry events, costs covered.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Whom you'll be working with</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/dasha-vyazemskaya/">Dasha</a>, our BDR Lead, who coaches you day to day</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/cliftonlobo/">Clifton</a>, our VP Global Sales</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/inga-schwarz/">Inga</a>, our pioneer AE in the OEM market segment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/sebastian-schaal/">Seba</a>, one of our founders, supporting the OEM go-to-market team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/maxhungenbach/">Max</a>, our Revenue Operations Team Lead, and his team</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Why Luminovo</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Measurable product impact: our procurement intelligence shows OEMs where they pay above market and which parts put production at risk</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A clear, written path from BDR to Account Executive</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI is part of how we work, from our MCP integrations to the agents our own teams build</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Psychological safety, honest feedback, an international and remote-first team</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Just so you know – we purposefully did not create a standard list of minimum qualifications for this role. We care much more about your motivation and ability to help us accelerate technical progress than we care just about your CV. If you're interested to find out more about why we banned requirements from our performance profiles – see <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/startup-grind/why-we-banned-requirements-from-our-job-descriptions-33a774e1a1c2">here</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>⚡️ About Luminovo</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Luminovo is the first electronics supply chain platform that unites all data, processes, and stakeholders in the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://luminovo.com/resources/blog/a-short-primer-on-the-electronics-industry?utm_campaign=employer_branding&amp;utm_source=candidate-traffic">trillion-dollar electronics industry</a>.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We fundamentally believe that technology is the best tool that humankind has developed to tackle the biggest challenges we face as a society today. And we want to do our share in accelerating technological progress. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>We bring innovations to life faster and cheaper by creating a more connected and resilient electronics supply chain.</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To date, over 400 active customers worldwide are working with us towards this shared goal. Supported by leading investors such as Cherry Ventures, General Catalyst/LaFamiglia, Chalfen Ventures, and others, we have <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://luminovo.com/resources/blog/luminovo-raises-eu11-million-in-seed-funding-to-fix-the-broken-electronics-value-chain-with-transformative-software-suite">raised more than €20 million</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our core principles: putting people first &amp; building great things</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a remote-first company headquartered in Munich, our brilliant team is spread across cities including Munich, New York, Austin, Calgary, Berlin, London, Valencia, Nairobi, and Verona, among others. 🌍</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our team includes a mix of product enthusiasts, people advocates, business masterminds, and engineering experts. Among us are graduates from institutions like Stanford University and the University of Cambridge, as well as talented individuals with unconventional CVs. What matters most is their drive to build great things.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We provide an authentic environment based on psychological safety to empower Luminerds from various backgrounds to succeed, grow, and focus on impact. Putting people first means that we deeply care about who our employees are, what makes them unique, and what they excel at. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">See what employees and candidates have to say about Luminovo on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.kununu.com/de/luminovo">kununu</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.glassdoor.de/Bewertungen/luminovo-ai-Bewertungen-E2039308.htm">Glassdoor</a>.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><hr><p>Compensation: €61,740 – €135,300 • Offers Equity • Offers Commission • Multiple Ranges</p><ul><li>Germany | Level 1 • On-Target Earnings €61,740 – €72,660 • Offers Equity • Offers Commission</li><li>Germany | Level 2 • On-Target Earnings €83,580 – €99,900 • Offers Equity • Offers Commission</li><li>Germany | Level 3 • On-Target Earnings €114,300 – €135,300 • Offers Equity • Offers Commission</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/luminovo-gmbh/business-development-representative-dach-ai-supply-chain-saas-bdr-munich-73470","tags":["Revenue"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"🇩🇪 Munich (hybrid)","created_at":1795740014},{"slug":"senior-controllerin-berlin-179862","company_name":"YAZIO","title":"Senior Controller:in (m/w/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>HALLO</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">wir suchen eine:n <strong>Senior Controller:in (m/w/d)</strong>, um bei Yazio einzusteigen und im Zuge unseres weiteren Wachstums die volle Verantwortung für unser Controlling zu übernehmen.<em> </em>Du bringst Struktur, Sorgfalt und fundiertes Fachwissen in unseren Monatsabschluss, die Buchhaltungsprozesse und die internen Kontrollen ein und setzt damit den Maßstab dafür, wie Controlling bei Yazio funktioniert.<em> </em>Mit rund 150 Mitarbeitenden wirken sich deine Entscheidungen zum Aufbau des Monatsabschlusses und zur Gestaltung der Buchhaltung langfristig aus. Diese bestimmen mit, wie das Finance-Team in den kommenden Jahren arbeitet.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du bist dafür verantwortlich, unsere zentralen Buchhaltungs- und Controlling-Prozesse kontinuierlich weiterzuentwickeln und zu verbessern. Du sorgst für korrekte und fristgerechte Finanzberichterstattung und bist die interne Anlaufstelle für fachliche Bilanzierungs- und Rechnungslegungsthemen.<em> </em>In enger Zusammenarbeit mit FP&amp;A, Legal, Operations und externen Partnern unterstützt du sowohl die operative Umsetzung im Tagesgeschäft als auch komplexe Bilanzierungsfragen zu neuen Produkten und Transaktionen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Diese Stelle ist zu 100 % remote und steht Bewerber:innen mit Wohnsitz in Deutschland, Spanien, Portugal oder dem Vereinigten Königreich offen.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>DEINE AUFGABEN</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Den Monatsabschluss von Anfang bis Ende aufbauen, verantworten und vorantreiben und gemeinsam mit Accounting und zentralen Stakeholdern eine schnelle, präzise und gut koordinierte Finanzberichterstattung sicherstellen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prüfung und Freigabe von Rückstellungen, Stichtagsbuchungen, Abstimmungen und Berichtspaketen für die Geschäftsleitung und den Bereich FP&amp;A</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Als zentrale Anlaufstelle für Fragen zur Rechnungslegung fungieren und neue Geschäftsmodelle, Verträge sowie komplexe Bilanzierungssachverhalte unterstützen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technische Rechnungslegungsdokumentation und Positionspapiere entwickeln und pflegen (z. B. Umsatzrealisierung, Aktivierung, Leasingverhältnisse und andere komplexe Themen)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Externe Partner wie Buchhalter:innen, Steuerberater:innen und Wirtschaftsprüfer:innen steuern und koordinieren und dabei für eine hohe Qualität der Dokumentation und eine reibungslose Zusammenarbeit sorgen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interne Kontrollen kontinuierlich stärken, indem du Auffälligkeiten erkennst, offene Punkte nachverfolgst und die Wirksamkeit der Kontrollen langfristig verbesserst</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prozess- und Systemverbesserungen vorantreiben, um manuellen Aufwand zu reduzieren, die Effizienz im Abschlussprozess zu steigern und skalierbare, gut dokumentierte Workflows aufzubauen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">KI-Werkzeuge für Analysen, Abweichungserklärungen, Audit-Vorbereitung und Recherchen in der Rechnungslegung einsetzen und dabei die kritische Prüfung sowie die Verantwortung für die Ergebnisse übernehmen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Eine moderne, skalierbare Finanzfunktion durch Automatisierung, Standardisierung und kontinuierliche Verbesserung aufbauen</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>DEIN PROFIL</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mehrjährige praktische Erfahrung in Buchhaltung, Controlling oder Finanzberichterstattung, idealerweise in schnell wachsenden Unternehmen mit zunehmender Komplexität</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Vorerfahrung in der Leitung oder Koordination eines kleinen Buchhaltungsteams ist von Vorteil</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fundierte Kenntnisse des deutschen HGB; IFRS-Erfahrung ist von Vorteil</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nachweisliche Verantwortung für den gesamten Monatsabschluss, mit Blick auf Richtigkeit, Vollständigkeit und eine hohe Qualität der Berichterstattung</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ausgeprägtes Verständnis für interne Kontrollen sowie die Fähigkeit, Risiken proaktiv zu erkennen, Kontrollen zu konzipieren und Prozesse kontinuierlich zu verbessern</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fortgeschrittene DATEV-Kenntnisse und sicherer Umgang mit Buchhaltungssystemen und Finanzdaten</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sicher im Umgang mit KI-Werkzeugen zur Steigerung der Produktivität (z. B. für Recherche, Dokumentation, Anomalieerkennung und Unterstützung bei der Berichterstattung), verbunden mit ausgeprägtem kritischen Urteilsvermögen bei der Bewertung der Ergebnisse</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strukturierte, dokumentationsorientierte Arbeitsweise mit einem klaren Fokus auf Prüfbarkeit und Transparenz</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ausgeprägter Wille zur Prozessverbesserung und ein gutes Gespür für Ineffizienzen und skalierbare Lösungen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nachweisliche Erfahrung im Umgang mit Stakeholdern und in der Zusammenarbeit mit externen Buchhalter:innen, Steuerberater:innen und Wirtschaftsprüfer:innen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wachstumsorientiertes Mindset und die Bereitschaft, sich laufend über Änderungen in Rechnungslegung und Steuerrecht zu informieren (z. B. HGB, Umsatzsteuer und IFRS)</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WARUM WIR?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ein spannendes Produkt mit Millionen von Nutzer:innen in über 150 Ländern, angetrieben von unserer Mission, die Welt durch gesunde Ernährung zu verändern</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ein Remote-First-Ansatz: Du arbeitest zu 100 % von zu Hause, nutzt einen Coworking-Space oder arbeitest für mehrere Wochen pro Jahr aus dem Ausland</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">30 Urlaubstage zum Entspannen und neue Energie tanken sowie 5 Kinderkrankentage, wenn dein Kind dich braucht</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Eine fokussierte Kultur, in der Effizienz wichtiger ist als lange Arbeitstage – keine Überstunden, und wenn doch, bekommst du die Zeit zurück!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ein Umfeld mit großer Wirkung, in dem deine Arbeit echte Veränderungen bewirkt – mit kurzen Entscheidungswegen und ohne Mikromanagement</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Eine Teamkultur, in der Ehrgeiz und Balance Hand in Hand gehen, getragen von starker Verbundenheit – vom komplett bezahlten Unternehmens-Retreat bis hin zu Teamtreffen und virtuellen Kaffeepausen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tools und Support, damit du deine beste Arbeit leisten kannst: MacBook, Monitor und ein jährliches Weiterbildungsbudget von 1.000 €, plus regelmäßiges Feedback und Unterstützung bei deiner Karriereentwicklung</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ein wirklich internationales Team mit Englisch als Unternehmenssprache und einem gemeinsamen Engagement für Wachstum und Wohlbefinden – unterstützt von Sunday Supplements und Nilo Health</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Vielfalt und Inklusion</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bei YAZIO sind wir überzeugt, dass Vielfalt Innovation antreibt. Wir setzen uns für ein inklusives Umfeld ein, in dem sich alle wertgeschätzt und gestärkt fühlen, unabhängig von Geschlechtsidentität, ethnischer Herkunft, Religion, Alter, sexueller Orientierung oder Behinderung. Wir schätzen unterschiedliche Perspektiven und ermutigen Menschen mit ganz verschiedenen Lebenswegen aktiv, sich bei uns zu bewerben.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>DU WILLST BEI UNS EINSTEIGEN?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du möchtest YAZIO aufs nächste Level bringen und Menschen weltweit zu einem gesünderen Leben verhelfen? Dann freuen wir uns darauf, von dir zu hören! Bitte sende uns:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deinen Lebenslauf auf Englisch</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ein paar Zeilen (oder ein kurzes Video, falls dir das lieber ist) darüber, wer du bist und warum du bei YAZIO arbeiten möchtest</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Weitere Unterlagen, die deine Arbeit zeigen (z. B. dein LinkedIn-Profil, Portfolio)</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/yazio/senior-controllerin-berlin-179862","tags":["Finance"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1795740013},{"slug":"senior-product-designer-berlin-50865","company_name":"Klim","title":"Senior Product Designer (m/f/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The team at Klim is building the operating system for regenerative agriculture. We help farms restore their soil - and turn that into real, measurable business value for the food companies, banks and insurers who depend on it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re a Berlin-based agritech startup backed by $22M in Series A funding, partnering with global food leaders such as Nestlé and ADM to build supply chain resilience through regenerative agriculture. Since 2020, we’ve supported +4,000  farmers managing over 900,000 hectares.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join our incredible team of 80+ dedicated people across Germany, the UK, Poland and Czechia to help build a more sustainable, resilient food system and drive real climate impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your mission:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the design experience of Klim end to end, and build the AI-augmented design process that lets a small design team and product managers ship coherent, high-quality work at scale. You'll do the hardest design work yourself and raise the level of everyone who designs around you. This means it is a player/coach role with <strong>60% hands-on design</strong> and <strong>40% building the system and process</strong> around you.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product experience:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the end-to-end experience across farmer and partner journeys, from onboarding through assessment, planning and improvement, verification and reporting and paymnet, shaping journeys and value moments with product managers, not only interfaces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design the most complex and brand-critical work, from wireframes and flows to polished, high-fidelity interaction and visual design.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cut farmer effort, with a focus on "enter once, used everywhere" data capture, simpler onboarding and self-serve help.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run continuous research, usability testing and A/B tests with farmers and partners, and track experience metrics (activation, task completion, time-to-value, satisfaction) with product and analytics.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI-augmented design process:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own and deliver Klim's AI-augmented design model maintaining highest quality while enabling others to deliver simpler design needs under your guidance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the canonical design system with engineering: components and page templates, with code as the source of truth and Figma kept in sync.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define the handoff contract and the automated and human coherence checks, using AI tooling (e.g. Claude Code, Claude Design, Figma, Storybook) and rules AI tools can follow.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Measure and improve the process: self-serve share, first-pass coherence, review time, engineering rework and ticket-to-design lead time.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Engineering efficiency and quality:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with engineering leads to simplify and standardise how UI is built, so new features reuse proven patterns instead of starting from scratch.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reduce design-related rework by making requirements, states and edge cases explicit before build.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Govern the intake of new patterns and log any exceptions, so the system grows deliberately rather than drifting.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Coach:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enable product managers to design simpler elements well within the system through templates, patterns, content rules and review.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build design rituals (critique, design reviews, a shared quality bar) and make the case for design decisions with evidence across product, engineering and commercial teams.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you bring:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years in product design, including senior or lead roles owning complex B2B or data-heavy products end to end.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional interaction and visual design craft, with mastery of Figma. You'll personally deliver the most complex and brand-critical work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A portfolio that shows product-level impact (engagement, adoption, satisfaction), not only interface quality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven ability to improve engagement and strong plus for experience running A/B tests and product experiments and strong research skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience building and running a design system with engineering, ideally in React and Storybook, with tokens and components treated as code.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on use of AI tools in design and delivery (e.g. Claude, Figma AI or similar), and a clear view of where they help and where they don't.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of designing processes others adopt, coaching designers and enabling non-designers, while still doing strong hands-on work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear communication with farmers, engineers and executives alike.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have:</strong></p><u