lich</p></li><li><p>Arbeitsmix: 95% Remote (nur in Deutschland möglich)</p></li><li><p>Wichtig: Bereitschaft zur <span style="color:#5D566C">SÜ2 nach § 9 SÜG Geheim/Sabotageschutz</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><span style="color:#a9c23f">DEINE MISSION</span></h3><p>Im Projekt geht es darum, eine clusterübergreifende Service-Mesh-Architektur auf Basis von Linkerd für verteilte Cloud- und Edge-Infrastrukturen im öffentlichen Sektor zu entwickeln. Ziel des Projekts ist es, eine sichere, resiliente und interoperable Vernetzung unterschiedlicher Kubernetes-Cluster und Edge-Systeme in einem multinationalen Umfeld zu ermöglichen.</p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Die Aufgaben im Detail:</p><ul><li><p>Konzeption und prototypische Umsetzung sicherer Multicluster-Verbindungen ohne Offenlegung der Kubernetes-API</p></li><li><p>Evaluierung und Konzeption clusterübergreifender Vertrauens- und Identitätsmodelle auf Basis von SPIFFE/SPIRE Federation</p></li><li><p>Aufbau von Testumgebungen, Durchführung und Auswertung von Netzwerktests sowie Ableitung technischer Optimierungen</p></li><li><p>Integration von virtuellen Maschinen, Servern und Single-Node-Edge-Geräten mittels Linkerd Mesh Expansion</p></li><li><p>Definition von Schnittstellen zu externen Diensten und Vorbereitung systemübergreifender Interoperabilitätstests</p></li><li><p>Erstellung von Deployment-Leitfäden und Referenzkonfigurationen (z. B. Helm Charts, Open Component Model)</p></li><li><p>Prototypische Entwicklung von Kubernetes-CRDs und Controllern zur Cluster-Vernetzung und Verwaltung von Vertrauensbeziehungen</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><span style="color:#A9C23F">MUST-HAVES FÜR DIESE POSITION</span></h3><ul><li><p>Mindestens 2 Jahre Erfahrung mit Linkerd und fundiertes Verständnis der technischen Implementierung</p></li><li><p>Mindestens 2 Jahre Erfahrung in der Softwareentwicklung mit Rust und Go (Golang)</p></li><li><p>Mindestens 2 Jahre Erfahrung mit Kubernetes und Platform Engineering</p></li><li><p>Englisch als Arbeitssprache</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><span style="color:#A9C23F">DEIN NEUER PROJEKTEINSATZ</span></h3><ul><li><p><strong>Flexible Arbeitszeiten:</strong> Aufgaben können zeitlich flexibel erledigt werden.</p></li><li><p><strong>Remote-Möglichkeit:</strong> Ortsunabhängiges Arbeiten, z. B. im Homeoffice oder mobil.</p></li><li><p><strong>Freie Projektwahl:</strong> Projekte werden passend zum Profil und zu den Interessen ausgewählt.</p></li><li><p><strong>Selbstbestimmte Organisation:</strong> Eigenständige Planung und Strukturierung der Arbeit.</p></li><li><p><strong>Fairer Austausch:</strong> Klare Kommunikation und wertschätzende Zusammenarbeit auf Augenhöhe.</p></li></ul><p><span style="color:#ffffff">#LI-DNI</span></p> <br> <p>Wenn du Interesse und aktuell freie Kapazitäten hast, freuen wir uns auf deine Bewerbung. Unser Recruiting-Team – rund um Alicja Okuniewicz, Anna-Lena Röcker und Jörg Becker – freut sich darauf, mit dir ins Gespräch zu kommen.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><div style="display: flex;" class="pm-columns"><div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; flex: 1; padding: 0 0.5em" class="pm-column"><figure style="text-align:right;"><img style="width:258px" alt="Jörg, Anna-Lena und Alicja" src="https://recruitee-main.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/lv19nvpf3b2hlkgwwdbvs5uyu8mkdn/Recruiting_Homepage-5_Quatrat_ohne_01.png"><figcaption>Jörg, Anna-Lena und Alicja</figcaption></figure></div><div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; flex: 1; padding: 0 0.5em" class="pm-column"><p><strong><span style="color:#A9C23F">virtual7 Recruiting-Team</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#5A5F72">Alicja Okuniewicz, Anna-Lena Röcker und Jörg Becker</span><br>+49 721 619017 31</p><p><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ----- ----- style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></div></div><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><figure style="text-align:center;"><img style="width:893px" src="https://recruitee-main.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/m4an4ut56ythcp1kaugfsht567rwhc/christian.png"></figure><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/virtual7-gmbh/remote-senior-service-mesh-engineer-linkerd-multicluster-bonn-253963","tags":["Customer Cluster Defense & Public Security","Remote"],"job_types":["Experienced","freelance"],"location":"Homeoffice","created_at":1795739496},{"slug":"senior-backend-engineer-engineering-manufacturing-systems-berlin-418958","company_name":"TYTAN Technologies GmbH","title":"Senior Backend Engineer - Engineering & Manufacturing Systems (f/m/d)","description":"<h4>TYTAN Technologies</h4><p><span style="color:#121317">The </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">PACE</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> is fast. The expectations are high. The contribution matters. Working at TYTAN is more than a job, this is a mission. We push boundaries, think big, and hold ourselves to the highest standard. Our mission and values guide everything we do, and we're looking for people who are driven by ownership, embrace challenges, and are energized by meaningful work. If you're motivated by impact and thrive in dynamic environments, you'll fit right in.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#121317">At </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">TYTAN</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">, we aim to set a global standard in autonomous air defense with AI-driven, cost-efficient systems that counter unmanned aerial threats at scale. We protect people. We protect critical infrastructure. We protect European sovereignty.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#121317">We are seeking an experienced and hands-on </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">Senior Backend Engineer, Engineering &amp; Manufacturing Systems</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> to own the software behind our end-of-line testing. You own the service that orchestrates test plans across stations, talks to PLCs, scanners and measurement equipment, provisions every unit and records what was tested. Every product and variant we build passes through it, and when it stops, the line stops. This is not a classic application backend: your system sits between software, hardware and the shop floor.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong>Your roadmap to make an impact</strong></h4><ul><li><p><strong>Test orchestration:</strong> Own the service end to end: API, test plan engine, state machines for units, jobs and plans, persistence, events and deployment</p></li><li><p><strong>Shop floor integration:</strong> Integrate PLCs, station middleware, 3D scanners and measurement and calibration equipment through robust interfaces with clear timeouts, retries and error handling</p></li><li><p><strong>Iterative tests:</strong> Closed feedback loops between the test runtime and the station, such as calibration where the station controls timing and the service computes the next step</p></li><li><p><strong>Products and variants:</strong> Model products, variants, test plans and tolerances so that new products and process changes become configuration, not code</p></li><li><p><strong>Provisioning and records:</strong> Integrate PKI and ERP to provision every unit and produce signed, auditable test records</p></li><li><p><strong>Line reliability:</strong> Offline tolerance at the station, idempotent operations, safe deployments during production and fast incident response</p></li><li><p><strong>Testability:</strong> Clean architecture and emulators for stations and devices, so changes are proven before they reach the line</p></li><li><p><strong>Observability:</strong> Structured logging, metrics and tracing that show what is wrong on the line before operators notice</p></li><li><p><strong>On the floor:</strong> Work with production engineers, quality and station suppliers, and turn process changes into software quickly</p></li></ul> <br> <ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Degree in Computer Science or a related field, or equivalent experience</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">5+ years of backend engineering in production</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Expert Python: typing, asyncio, a modern web framework such as FastAPI, and pytest as a daily tool</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Strong grasp of software architecture: clean architecture, hexagonal (ports and adapters) and domain-driven design, applied in real codebases</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">State machines and workflow orchestration for long-running processes, with idempotency, retries and consistent recovery after failures</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">API design: REST and OpenAPI, signed webhooks, versioning and backward compatibility with external suppliers</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">MongoDB in depth: document modelling, schema versioning, indexing and migrations on live data</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Security in production systems: certificate signing flows, mTLS and API authentication</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Observability and operations: OpenTelemetry or similar, alerting, incident response; Docker and Kubernetes on premises or at the edge</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Fluent in English; German is a plus on the shop floor</span></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Beneficial</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Experience with systems that talk to hardware or the shop floor: manufacturing test, MES, industrial automation or lab automation</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Industrial integration: OPC UA, Modbus TCP or comparable PLC interfaces, plus serial and Ethernet device communication</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">MES, traceability and genealogy in manufacturing</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Test executive frameworks such as NI TestStand or OpenHTF</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">ERP integration</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Calibration and metrology processes</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Regulated manufacturing such as aerospace or automotive quality standards</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Operator interfaces for production stations</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong><span style="color:#121317">Why TYTAN?</span></strong></h4><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Build technology with real operational impact:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Develop autonomous defense systems designed to protect lives and strengthen Europe’s security</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Shape scalable defense capabilities:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Work on solutions built for mass deployment, cost efficiency, resilience, and reliable production at scale</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Contribute to networked air defense:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Help integrate our systems into multi-layered defense architectures alongside sensors, command systems, and effectors</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Develop for real-world operations:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Build capabilities together with end users and improve them continuously based on direct operational feedback</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Move fast and take ownership:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Work in a focused, high-performance team where decisions are made quickly and in