ger.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Stay close to system design and architecture of our event-driven services (Ruby, Kafka), and set the technical bar across your teams.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Raise the bar on ownership: documentation, runbooks, observability and on-call.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Champion AI-assisted engineering across your teams: coding agents, AI code review, test generation and documentation. Measure which practices improve delivery and quality.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Define safe guardrails for AI use where money moves: human review, test coverage and auditability stay non-negotiable.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><strong>Workplace: </strong></p><p>We are a remote-first company with teams located around the Globe and a HQ in Berlin. </p> <br> <p><strong>Who you are:</strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">An experienced Engineering Manager who has led multiple teams or a team of senior engineers.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Required:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> hands-on background in payments. You've built or run payment systems in production, including PSP integrations, refunds and chargebacks, reconciliation and recurring billing.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You understand PCI DSS, SCA/3DS and what it takes to keep money flows </span>auditable.</p></li><li><p>An<span style="color:#000000"> engineer at heart, with experience in event-driven distributed systems (Kafka or similar) and strong skills in a modern backend language. Ruby is a plus.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You're comfortable working across teams and departments, and you communicate clearly in writing in English.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You use AI tools in your own day-to-day work, not just in theory. You've helped a team adopt them, an