>Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/arsipa-gmbh/ingenieurin-qualitatssicherung-wohnungsbau-im-grossraum-lubeck-sigeko-ingenieure-485452","tags":["sigeko – Ingenieure"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Lübeck, Schleswig-Holstein, Deutschland","created_at":1795728702},{"slug":"service-designer-consultant-senior-consultant-deutschlandweit-munich-227914","company_name":"Infosys Consulting Europe","title":"Service Designer - Consultant / Senior Consultant- Deutschlandweit","description":"<p><strong>Service Designer </strong></p><p><em>Technology Transformation practice </em></p><p><em>Anywhere in Germany, with travel availability</em></p><p><em>Consultant/Senior Consultant <br><br></em><strong>About Us</strong></p><p>You want to boost your career and collaborate with expert, talented colleagues to solve and deliver against our clients' most important challenges? We are growing and are looking for people to join our team. You'll be part of an entrepreneurial, high-growth environment of 300.000 employees. Our dynamic organization allows you to work across functional business pillars, contributing your ideas, experiences, diverse thinking, and a strong mindset. Are you ready?<br><br><strong>The Team</strong> </p><p>Our Technology Transformation practice is helping organizations all over the world transform their operating model to succeed in the new normal – scaling up digitization and cloud transformation programs, optimizing costs, and accelerating value realization. Our solutions focus on the big-ticket value items on the C-Suite agenda, providing a deep link between business and IT to help you lead with influence beyond the back-office remit. For more information and details on the services we provide and the clients we serve, please visit or <a href="https://www.infosys.com/services/consulting/offerings/technology-transformation.html" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external">careers page.</a><br><br><strong>The role </strong></p><p>As a Service Designer at Infosys Consulting, you help our clients understand what their customers really need and turn those insights into services that work seamlessly across every touchpoint – digital and physical, frontstage and backstage. You make the entire customer journey smooth and enjoyable for users and successful for the business, driving satisfaction, retention and long-term growth.</p><p>You bring a solid foundation in human-centered design, CX strategy and digital transformation, and you understand how service experiences connect to the client’s marketing, CRM, customer care and operations. Working directly with client stakeholders, you lay the groundwork for a holistic service and CX strategy, establish standards, processes and ways of working, and build the client’s own capability.</p><p><strong>Key Responsibilities : </strong></p><h3>Service &amp; CX Strategy</h3><ul><li>Define a service vision and CX strategy that delivers consistent, high-quality experiences across all channels and aligns with business objectives.</li><li>Translate business goals into service principles, experience goals and measurable KPIs (e.g. NPS, CSAT, CES, retention)</li><li>Map and re-orchestrate the service ecosystem along the customer life cycle using ecosystem maps and stakeholder maps</li><li>Develop service propositions and value propositions together with business owners</li><li>Define the roadmap of guidelines, trainings and key projects needed to realize the strategy</li><li>Shape the target operating model and team structure for service design and CX on the client side</li><li>Work with leadership to embed Service Design and Design Thinking in the company’s culture</li></ul><h3>Insight Management &amp; Customer Understanding</h3><ul><li>Turn customer data, research and behavior into actionable insights in collaboration with research and analytics teams.</li><li>Synthesize qualitative and quantitative data into personas, jobs-to-be-done, mental models and insight statements</li><li>Use NPS, satisfaction and operational metrics to assess the current experience and spot patterns, trends and pain points</li><li>Present data-driven recommendations that improve retention and satisfaction</li><li>Set up an insight and requirements pipeline that continuously feeds product, channel and solution owners</li></ul><h3>Journey Mapping &amp; Service Blueprinting</h3><ul><li>Make the end-to-end service visible and design how it should work in future – for customers, employees and systems.</li><li>Facilitate as-is customer journey maps and service blueprints across channels, including frontstage, backstage and supporting processes</li><li>Identify moments of truth, breakpoints and improvement opportunities online and offline</li><li>Design to-be journeys and blueprints across multiple applications as well as in depth for specific services</li><li>Connect journey and blueprint work to process, organizational and technology changes</li></ul><h3>Co-Creation, Ideation &amp; Prototyping</h3><ul><li>Lead the double-diamond process from problem framing to tested solution together with clients and their customers.</li><li>Plan and facilitate co-creation workshops, design sprints and ideation sessions with cross-functional teams</li><li>Frame problems with How-Might-We questions, opportunity areas and design challenges</li><li>Create and test service prototypes – storyboards, service walkthroughs, desktop walkthroughs, role-play and click dummies</li><li>Run experiments and pilots, measure impact and iterate towards scalable solutions</li></ul><h3>Service Standards &amp; Guidelines</h3><ul><li>Initiate and support standards that ensure high service quality across websites, native apps, phone, email, chat and in-person support.</li><li>Create service design playbooks, journey and blueprint libraries, persona sets and design principles</li><li>Establish service standards, benchmarks and end-to-end testing approaches</li><li>Set up quality assurance processes to monitor and evaluate customer interactions</li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Degree in Service Design, Interaction/UX Design, Design Management, Business, Psychology or a related field</li><li><strong>Consultant:</strong> 3–5 years of experience in service design, CX or UX, ideally in consulting or an in-house design team</li><li><strong>Senior Consultant:</strong> 5–8 years of experience, including leading projects and client workstreams</li><li><strong>Hands-on command of core service design methods:</strong> stakeholder and ecosystem mapping, personas, customer journey mapping, service blueprinting, co-creation and service prototyping</li><li>Experience with design research (interviews, contextual inquiry, observation, diary studies) and synthesis (affinity mapping, insight clustering)</li><li>Ability to link customer insight with business objectives, KPIs and business cases</li><li>Strong workshop facilitation and stakeholder management skills, from operational teams to C-level</li><li>Confident with collaboration and visualisation tools such as Miro, Mural, Figma or similar</li><li>Ability to integrate AI tools throughout every stage of the design process, from research and insight generation to ideation, prototyping, testing, and service optimization, enhancing both efficiency and innovation.</li><li>Excellent communication and storytelling skills in both GERMAN and ENGLISH</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Preferred/Desirable experience </strong><br></p><ul><li>Experience in CX strategy and digital transformation programmes</li><li><strong>Knowledge of adjacent areas on the client side:</strong> marketing, CRM and loyalty, customer care and contact centres</li><li>Experience designing omnichannel services that combine digital and physical touchpoints</li><li>Preferred tool proficiency: Miro, Figma, FigJam, Claude Code</li><li>Familiarity with CX metrics (NPS, CSAT, CES) and Voice-of-Customer programmes</li><li>Exposure to agile delivery, Lean UX and product operating models</li><li>Experience applying AI and GenAI in services or CX operations</li><li>Experience building design capabilities, playbooks or design systems at client organisations</li><li>Industry experience in e.g. retail, automotive, financial services, telecommunications, utilities or the public sector</li><li>Certification in Design Thinking, Service Design (e.g. SDN) or agile methods</li></ul><h3>Level differentiation</h3><p><strong>Consultant:</strong> delivers service design work within a project, applies methods confidently and facilitates workshops with guidance</p><p><strong>Senior Consultant:</strong> owns workstreams and client relationships, shapes the approach, coaches junior team members and contributes to proposals and business development<br><br><em>Given that this is just a short snapshot of the role we encourage you to apply even if you don't meet all the requirements listed above. We are looking for individuals who strive to make an impact and are eager to learn. If this sounds like you and you feel you have the skills and experience required, then please apply now.</em></p><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><p><strong>About Infosys Consulting</strong></p><p>Be part of a globally renowned management consulting firm on the front-line of industry disruption and at the cutting edge of technology.&nbsp; We work with market leading brands across sectors. Our culture is inclusive and entrepreneurial.&nbsp;Being a mid-size consultancy within the scale of Infosys gives us the global reach to partner with our clients throughout their transformation journey.</p><p>Our core values, IC-LIFE, form a common code that helps us move forward. IC-LIFE stands for Inclusion, <strong>Equity </strong>and Diversity, Client, Leadership, Integrity, Fairness, and Excellence. To learn more about Infosys Consulting and our values, please visit our .</p><p>Within Europe, we a