&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; London (Hybrid) | &lt;strong&gt;Practice Area:&lt;/strong&gt; Financial Crime, Risk, Regulation, &amp;amp; Financial Crime | &lt;strong&gt;Type:&lt;/strong&gt; Permanent&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape the future of third-party risk management, lead complex transformation programmes and help financial institutions build resilient operating models, incident response capabilities and effective risk management frameworks.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;The Role&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Capco, we&#39;re looking for a Managing Principal to play a key role in shaping and delivering Third-Party Risk Management (TPRM), incident response and operational resilience transformation for leading financial services clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work with senior stakeholders to define transformation strategies, design and implement target operating models, and develop the processes, governance and capabilities organisations need to effectively assess, monitor and manage third-party risks. You&#39;ll take ownership of complex client engagements, guiding programmes from initial assessment and strategic design through to implementation, embedding sustainable improvements and delivering measurable business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A key focus will be helping clients strengthen their ability to prepare for, manage and respond to third-party incidents and crises. This includes shaping incident response strategies, enhancing crisis management frameworks, developing third-party risk assessment capabilities, and overseeing crisis simulation and scenario testing to validate organisational preparedness and resilience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Managing Principal, you&#39;ll also contribute to the growth of Capco&#39;s risk and resilience consulting capabilities, building trusted relationships with senior client stakeholders, identifying new business opportunities, supporting proposals and developing high-performing consulting teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll champion the responsible adoption of approved AI tools and automation to improve third-party risk assessments, monitoring, incident analysis and reporting, ensuring appropriate governance, human oversight and accountability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Third-Party Risk Transformation:&lt;/strong&gt; Shape and deliver complex TPRM transformation programmes, working with senior stakeholders to define strategies, assess current capabilities, establish future-state visions, develop transformation roadmaps and oversee implementation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design Operating Models &amp;amp; Capabilities:&lt;/strong&gt; Direct the design and implementation of TPRM target operating models, governance structures, policies, processes and controls, ensuring clear accountability, effective risk management and sustainable operational capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enhance Third-Party Risk Assessment Frameworks:&lt;/strong&gt; Oversee the development and implementation of third-party risk assessment methodologies, including supplier due diligence, criticality assessments, inherent and residual risk evaluation, concentration risk, dependency mapping and ongoing monitoring.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strengthen Incident Response &amp;amp; Crisis Testing:&lt;/strong&gt; Shape third-party incident and crisis management strategies, including response frameworks, escalation arrangements, contingency planning, crisis simulation exercises, scenario testing and recovery capabilities to improve organisational resilience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Client Relationships, Growth &amp;amp; Innovation:&lt;/strong&gt; Build trusted relationships with senior client stakeholders, identify and develop new consulting opportunities, contribute to proposals and business development, mentor consulting teams and promote responsible AI-enabled approaches to risk management and transformation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Significant experience leading complex transformation programmes across third-party risk management, operational risk, incident response or operational resilience within financial services or consulting, with a track record of delivering measurable outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Extensive experience designing and implementing TPRM target operating models, governance frameworks, risk management processes and organisational capabilities, from strategic design through to operational implementation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In-depth experience developing and enhancing third-party risk assessment frameworks, including risk methodologies, supplier due diligence, risk mitigation, monitoring and management of critical third-party dependencies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience shaping and delivering third-party incident response and crisis management capabilities, including crisis governance, escalation processes, scenario testing, simulation exercises, contingency planning and recovery strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to engage and influence senior stakeholders, lead multidisciplinary consulting teams, manage complex client engagements and contribute to business development, with an interest in using approved AI tools and automation to improve transformation outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Bonus Points For&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience leading enterprise-wide TPRM transformation initiatives, including organisational redesign, process optimisation, governance enhancement, capability development and implementation of risk management platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Knowledge of third-party incident and crisis management frameworks, including third-party failure scenarios, crisis simulation exercises, tabletop testing and resilience assurance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with UK operational resilience expectations, including FCA/PRA requirements, important business services, impact tolerances and severe but plausible scenario testing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience developing consulting propositions, supporting sales opportunities, managing senior client relationships and contributing to the growth of risk and resilience advisory services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Exposure to AI-enabled risk monitoring, incident analytics, workflow automation or digital transformation programmes, with an understanding of responsible AI governance and human oversight.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Why Join Capco&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deliver high-impact technology solutions for Tier 1 financial institutions.&lt;/p&gt;
