tions-london-165454","company_name":"9Fin","title":"Director of Engineering - Product Foundations","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About 9fin</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">9fin is the AI platform powering global debt markets — the world’s largest asset class at over $145 trillion.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Debt markets are vast, global, and mission-critical, yet still run on fragmented data, PDFs, and manual workflows. 9fin replaces this broken infrastructure with a single platform that centralises proprietary credit data, deep analysis, and high-value workflows across global markets.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, 9fin powers teams at 300+ blue-chip institutions worldwide, including global banks, asset managers, private equity firms, law firms, and advisors. The business is scaling at exceptional speed, with rapid expansion in the US and best-in-class retention driven by deep workflow adoption.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re at a defining inflection point. With proven product-market fit and strong, global market pull, 9fin is accelerating toward becoming the category-defining platform for debt markets worldwide.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>The Opportunity</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">9fin’s Engineering org has grown rapidly to more than 150 engineers across multiple tribes, and we are continuing to expand.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI sits at the centre of what we ship to customers and of how our teams design, build and release software. We are seeking a <strong>Director of Engineering</strong> to set the technical vision and lead multiple high-impact teams responsible for our <strong>Product Foundations</strong> area, the foundations (web and other distribution channels) that delivers 9fin to our customers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role requires a deeply technical, AI-first leader who owns delivery end to end and understands how engineering drives the commercial success of the business. You will <strong>lead by example</strong>, establishing a culture of <strong>engineering excellence</strong> where teams tackle complex challenges, innovate boldly, and grow their skills.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for an experienced leader with a proven track record of scaling both systems and teams. You will define architecture, drive strategy across the group, and empower leaders and ICs to deliver at scale while staying <strong>close enough to the details</strong> to mentor and inspire your teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Director for Product Foundations, your role is to amplify the impact of your teams, making strategic decisions that shape the long-term direction of the area. You will ensure reliability, enable rapid innovation, and create the conditions for lasting technical and cultural impact. You'll help shape how a 150+ person engineering org works in an AI-native way, and you'll be measured on what reaches customers and what it does for the business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product Foundations:</strong> Every 9fin product runs on the same core capabilities: authentication, entitlements, notifications and the other shared services that every customer touches and every product team relies on. Your customers are 9fin’s product engineering teams, and you’ll lead with a <strong>platform-as-a-product</strong> mindset: treat shared capabilities as products, with clear roadmaps, well-designed APIs and documentation, self-serve onboarding and defined SLOs, measuring success through adoption, reliability and developer satisfaction. Get this right and every squad ships faster and focuses on its own customers, every customer gets a seamless and secure experience, and 9fin can launch new products on foundations built to scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>What you’ll work on</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every day is different, but here’s a dose of the kind of things you’ll be doing:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide strategic &amp; technical leadership over multiple teams in the <strong>Product Foundations</strong> area, ensuring alignment with company objectives and technical direction.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and scale high-performing, cross-functional teams, and grow your Engineering Leads and ICs into stronger leaders with wider technical reach.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the long-term technical vision, driving architectural decisions that enable future growth and system evolution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Product, Design, Commercial and Customer teams to understand how your area drives revenue and retention, and prioritise the work that moves the business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with fellow Engineering leaders and leaders to align roadmaps, resolve cross-team dependencies and make shared decisions, succeeding together as one 9fin engineering team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Foster a culture of engineering excellence through mentorship, standard-setting, and championing robust engineering practices across teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own hiring for your area, partnering with the VP Engineering and our People and Talent teams to build strong, AI-fluent teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own delivery for the area end to end: set commitments with Product, track them, and be accountable for outcomes across large cross-team programmes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Oversee technical operations and incident response practices across teams, ensuring high system reliability and actionable learning from incidents.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify and drive systemic improvements to engineering velocity, platform reliability and security, building security in from the start and adopting tooling, including AI, where it measurably helps teams ship faster and safer.</p></li></ul><h1>About You</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role will be a great fit if you:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are a deeply technical engineering leader with a software development background and a track record of leading multiple teams and managers in complex, high-growth environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical in practice: Earn technical credibility with senior engineers: you review designs in depth, challenge architecture constructively, and can still get hands-on when needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have defined, owned and executed technical strategy, scaled systems, and tied engineering investment to business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have designed and evolved cross-functional engineering orgs as they scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have built or led internal platforms run as products: you engage your internal customers, prioritise based on their needs, and measure success through adoption, reliability and developer experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Think commercially: you understand how your work drives revenue and retention, and you balance customer experience, architecture and resilience accordingly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate clearly and influence across engineering, product, design, commercial and executive leadership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are a collaborative peer who builds strong partnerships with other engineering leaders and puts 9fin’s success ahead of team boundaries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop senior engineering talent, build succession plans, and create an inclusive environment where leaders grow their impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver on commitments while raising operational maturity and reliability across a growing organisation.<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We