sfer pricing, intercompany agreements, and residence and substance requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Finance on tax accounting, forecasting, ERP configuration and cash tax planning, and review and sign off returns.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advise on corporate transactions: reorganisations, IP location, fundraising, M&amp;A and employee share schemes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Get ahead of change, from UK gambling tax changes to Pillar Two, and turn it into clear recommendations for senior management and commercial teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the governance a scaling group needs: SAO readiness, Corporate Criminal Offence procedures, a tax risk register, and a published tax strategy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage our external advisers and their fees, and represent Midnite with HMRC and other tax authorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Find and land opportunities, from R&amp;D tax credits to optimising our gambling taxes.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The next Midniter:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Holds a recognised tax and/or accountancy qualification (such as CTA, ADIT, ACA, ICAS, ACCA).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Has 10+ years' relevant experience, including top-tier advisory and several years in a senior in-house tax role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Has designed international structures and transfer pricing across multiple jurisdictions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Is commercial and turns complex analysis into clear recommendations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Is happy to be hands-on: writing memos, reviewing returns, and briefing senior management</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicates simply with founders, senior management, and non-tax teams, and enjoys teaching others.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manages advi