<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Action-focused:</strong> You find the right balance between seeking help and executing your own solutions, responding with pace to reasonable requests outside of the normal scope of work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience in supplier statement reconciliation: </strong>Experience of working in supplier payments/account payable</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>MS Excel proficient</strong><br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Desirable:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>G Suite experience</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Experience in the travel sector</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Experience of merchant acquirer statement reconciliation</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Experience of working with virtual credit cards</em></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The interview journey:</strong></p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Call with the Talent Partner (30 mins)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final stage interview with Hiring Managers (45 mins)</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Perks of joining us:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Company pension contributions at 5%.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Individualised training budget for you to learn on the job and level yourself up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Discounted holidays for you, your family and friends.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 days of holidays per annum (plus 8 public holidays) increases by 1 day for every second year of service, up to a maximum 30 days per annum.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to buy and sell annual leave.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cycle to work scheme, season ticket loan and eye care vouchers.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our commitment to inclusion</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At loveholidays, we focus on creating an inclusive environment where everyone can contribute, grow and succeed. We value the different perspectives, experiences and ideas each person brings, because they help us work better together, challenge our thinking and make stronger decisions.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>As we continue to grow and evolve, we want everyone to feel supported and able to do their best work. We’re also committed to making our hiring process accessible, so please let our Talent Acquisition team know if you need any adjustments at any stage.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/loveholidays/accounts-payable-executive-12-month-ftc-london-85292","tags":["Finance"],"job_types":["Contract"],"location":"London","created_at":1795740013},{"slug":"head-of-product-uk-sme-london-38785","company_name":"Taxfix","title":"Head of Product, UK SME","description":"<h2>Our story:</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every year millions of people are either filing their taxes in fear or giving up on their tax refund altogether. We're working on fixing that. Our intuitive app enables anyone, regardless of education or background, to file their taxes with newfound confidence.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Spread across Germany, Spain and the UK, the team at Taxfix Group with its brands Taxfix and Steuerbot, is a compassionate group of solution-finders. We speak our minds openly, and with over 400 professionals, including tax experts, developers, and IT security experts, we're rich in ideas and voices. The group has facilitated more than 3.5 billion euros in tax refunds for its customers since its founding in 2016.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The opportunity: <strong> </strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Freelancers, contractors, sole traders and small business owners deserve an easier way to run their business finances. This is the next big focus area for Taxfix in the UK, and this role will shape our future offerings for this segment. As Head of Product for UK Self-Employed &amp; SME, you will be responsible for understanding this customer deeply, setting the vision, shaping the roadmap, and rallying stakeholders to bring incredible customer experiences to life. This is a senior individual contributor role. You have no direct reports and you lead through vision, craft and influence. At Taxfix we call the people who own a problem from idea to shipped product, stretching across product, design and engineering with AI, <strong>builders</strong>. This is an opportunity to be a product leader and a builder.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Your responsibilities: </h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the vision, roadmap and outcomes.</strong> Set a clear product vision and strategy for UK self-employed and small business customers. Agree targets with leadership and your commercial partner and then own them and drive the key results. Make priorities clear and trade-offs visible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be the voice of the self-employed.</strong> Know these customers as well as anyone in the company, through direct contact, not distance. Be their ambassador in every decision.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own discovery.</strong> Lead problem and customer need discovery so the builder teams always have well-qualified, relevant work. Bring your own well-informed ideas, not only a response to a brief.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Take a product from proof to pillar.</strong> Find product-market fit, pour fuel on what works, and make smart build-vs-partner calls, using shared capabilities where it is faster and building where it is core.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive adoption and depth of engagement.</strong> Make this the product customers rely on all year, not once. Own activation, retention and how widely customers use what we offer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build the AI-native product.</strong> Have a clear point of view on where AI removes real load for the self-employed and for accountants, and push the team to build what was not possible only months ago.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run the team on experimentation and data.</strong> Make decisions with data, and with strategy and market judgement when the data is unclear. Speed to learning is a first-class metric you own.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be the commercial partner, not the commercial owner.</strong> Shape the proposition with your commercial partner: tiers, pricing, packaging and bundling. Translate the commercial ambition into a product that delivers it, push back clearly when the product path and the ask do not align, and lead launches together with marketing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build responsibly in a regulated space.</strong> Work with compliance, financial crime and tax experts so that what you ship meets regulatory standards and is accurate, explainable and safe, including the edge cases and the risks that come with AI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Set the bar for craft.</strong> Set direction for the teams you work with. Give them a vision sharp enough to act on and help remove handoffs and bottlenecks. Be entrepreneurial and lean in to build directly when needed. Credibility and influence matter more than authority.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p></li></ul><h2>Your profile: </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your track record</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have led product for a multi-team area, ideally for consumer or micro-SME customers, in a scale-up where you had fewer resources than you wanted and got things done by being hands-on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have taken a product from early traction to a real growth engine, with customers who rely on it, not just sign-ups. You can say why it worked, which metric moved and what you would do differently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in accounting, tax, or banking products is a strong plus, as is familiarity with UK tax, Making Tax Digital or HMRC-facing products. </p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You are a builder</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have built and shipped with AI yourself, not just written specs about it, and you know when to trust the output, when to edit it and when to reject it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You use AI every day, and you are credible with design and engineering because you have built something end to end.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How you work</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are measured by outcomes and decide with data, and with strategy and market judgement when the data is unclear. You believe experimentation is how products win and treat velocity as a metric that matters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You lead by influence: you have raised the bar for the people around you, with or without a team of your own, and people who worked with you got better.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You communicate clearly and concisely, with an ambitious vision for the product and a real curiosity about small businesses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a bias to action, give feedback directly, own your misses, and are respectful, honest and kind.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>Why Taxfix? </h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A chance to do meaningful, people-centric work with an international team of passionate professionals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Holistic well-being with free mental health coaching sessions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A monthly allowance to spend on an extensive range of services that you can use and roll over as flexibly as you like.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employee stock options for all employees—because everyone deserves to benefit from the success they help to create.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">30 annual vacation days and flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A generous learning budget to support your personal and professional development and guidance from our internal L&amp;D experts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work from abroad for up to six weeks every year. Just align with your team, and then enjoy your trip.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plenty of opportunities to socialise as a team. In addition to internal meetups, our international team hosts regular get-togethers—virtually and in person when possible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Free tax declaration filing, of course, through the Taxfix app—and internal support for all personal tax-related questions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have a four-legged friend in your life? We’re happy to have dogs join us in the office.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />Excited? So are we. Check out our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/taxfix/life/8684512c-424f-44de-8d07-6e6b516e3319/?viewAsMember=true"> <u>Life at Taxfix</u></a> page on LinkedIn to get a glimpse of our culture.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At Taxfix, we believe that incredible things happen when you have a wealth of perspectives and experiences. We're proudly committed to equal employment and development opportunities no matter your gender, race, religion, age, sexual orientation, colour, disability, or place of origin. To help mitigate any potential unconscious biases, we ask that you refrain from including your picture, age, or marital status on your CV. Let your experiences speak for themselves.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not sure if you meet all the requirements for this role? Please apply anyway. You might bring something special to the team that we hadn't considered previously.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/taxfix/head-of-product-uk-sme-london-38785","tags":["Product Management"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1795740013},{"slug":"satellite-mechanical-design-engineer-reading-327516","company_name":"Neworbit","title":"Satellite Mechanical Design Engineer","description":"<h2><strong>Company</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">NewOrbit builds satellites that fly in very low Earth orbit, below 300 km, along with the electric propulsion that keeps them there.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flying closer to Earth means sharper imagery from smaller optics, and an orbit that cleans itself: our satellites de-orbit within a month at end of life, leaving no debris.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our AURA family of RF gridded ion thrusters powers our own NEO-1 satellite, with first flight planned for Q3 2028, and is also offered to other operators.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Electric propulsion is what lets our satellites hold very low orbits, and our AURA RF gridded ion thruster is at the centre of it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Role Overview</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will design satellite structure and hardware, and help keep the satellite's full CAD assembly organised and under control as the design matures. Working within a small, multidisciplinary team, you will translate requirements into manufacturable designs and support their validation through prototyping and environmental testing.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and develop mechanical hardware for the satellite, including secondary structures (panels, brackets and component mounts), thermal-control hardware, cable and harness routing, and mechanisms. Primary structure experience is welcome.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work in the satellite's large 3D CAD assembly alongside the wider design team, using top-down design and skeleton models to keep interfaces, configurations and revisions in step as several designers work in the same model.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage assembly configuration, PLM data (3DEXPERIENCE ('3DX') or similar), bills of materials and engineering change control (ECO/ECR/ECN), so that models, drawings and interfaces stay consistent as changes are released.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run interference and clash checks and maintain the digital mock-up, working with each subsystem owner to allocate space and resolve conflicts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Produce fully dimensioned, manufacturing-ready drawings and interface control documents using GD&amp;T.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support design reviews (PDR and CDR) and qualification, working with structural and thermal engineers on analysis and verification planning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Optimise designs for manufacturability, cost, mass and reliability, working directly with manufacturers and suppliers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support prototype builds, integration and environmental test campaigns, iterating designs based on results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with electrical, software, systems and thermal engineers to integrate mechanical components into the satellite platform.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Required Skills &amp; Experience</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bachelor's degree in mechanical, aerospace or a related engineering discipline.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years' experience in mechanical design of aerospace, space or other high-reliability hardware, with strong 3D CAD skills (SolidWorks preferred; CATIA, NX or Creo also considered).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical application of GD&amp;T and experience producing manufacturing-ready drawings.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid grounding in mechanical design principles, materials and thermal management, with a working understanding of structural mechanics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated ability to design, build and test hardware, including troubleshooting and iteration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear communicator who is comfortable explaining and defending design decisions, and open to feedback and challenge in a fast-moving team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Preferred Experience</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Satellite or spacecraft design, ideally detailed design of secondary structures (panel and component mounting, thermal hardware, cable and harness routing). Primary structure experience is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in large, multi-person CAD assemblies, including top-down design, skeleton or master models, in-context references and configurations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with PLM or PDM systems (for example 3DEXPERIENCE ('3DX'), Windchill, Teamcenter, ENOVIA or SolidWorks PDM), configuration management, revision control and formal change processes (ECO/ECR/ECN).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working within formal engineering processes, such as design reviews, documented requirements and standards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hardware that has launched.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Basic FEA familiarity, MGSE or ground-support equipment design, and electromechanical packaging.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Why NewOrbit Space?</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pioneering space technology</strong> - Your work on our RF gridded ion thrusters and VLEO satellite platform will redefine satellite operations and challenge traditional LEO.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership and impact</strong> - You'll have a level of ownership that's rare in the space industry, and you'll take part in the full lifecycle of satellite technology.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equity and competitive salary</strong> - Alongside a competitive salary you receive a company ownership stake, so you share in the technology you help build and in our collective success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Comprehensive benefits</strong> - Private health insurance with dental and optical cover, and annual health check-ups.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hybrid working</strong> - One dedicated remote day per week.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Visa sponsorship and relocation support</strong> - We sponsor visas and provide relocation support for candidates moving to join us.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/neworbit/satellite-mechanical-design-engineer-reading-327516","tags":["Satellite"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Reading, UK","created_at":1795740012},{"slug":"deployment-strategist-london-205076","company_name":"Ankar","title":"Deployment Strategist - London","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>At Ankar, </strong>we’re building AI to transform industrial R&amp;D.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">From understanding the technology landscape and identifying new invention opportunities to accelerating R&amp;D and bringing products to market, we're inventing how innovation happens.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work with some of the world's leading enterprises across industries, helping them unlock the value of their knowledge, experts, technical expertise, inventions, and turn ideas into real-world impact. <strong>We're the builders of the new age of industrial innovation.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us at a unique moment of scale:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We've raised &gt;$24M to date from Tier-1 VCs like Atomico, Index Ventures, Norrsken, Daphni, and angels like the founders of Hugging Face, CEO of Datadog, and Leaders from DeepMind and OpenAI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're already working with the world's most innovative companies including Fortune 500 companies such as L'Oréal.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expanding our world-class team with alumni from Palantir, Amazon, and BCG to tackle the $1T+ innovation market. We're just getting started.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're growing rapidly, and looking for exceptional people to help us build what comes next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Deployment Strategist at Ankar, you'll help <strong>chart and build the art of the possible in enterprise R&amp;D.</strong> You'll work on the frontlines with some of the world's leading enterprises, tackling their most important innovation challenges and bringing together technology, product and business to deliver real world outcomes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your mission is to discover where Ankar can create extraordinary value for our customers, and make that value a reality.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll immerse yourself in complex organisations, develop a deep understanding of their people, science, priorities and challenges, and uncover opportunities others might miss.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll bring curiosity, product intuition, commercial instinct and the ability to connect with people at every level of an organisation, helping them challenge established ways of working, imagine what's possible, and turn that ambition into action.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This isn't a traditional consulting, customer success or technical implementation role. You'll be part strategist, part operator, part product thinker and part builder. You'll need to be equally comfortable working with end users to understand their day-to-day challenges, shaping a proposition with senior executives, and collaborating with engineers to build something that doesn't yet exist.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll own outcomes, not just deliverables. From shaping an initial pilot to driving adoption, demonstrating impact and identifying opportunities to expand, you'll play a critical role in building Ankar's most important customer partnerships.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You'll Do</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Discover and unlock customer value</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Immerse yourself in customers' businesses, workflows and strategic priorities to identify their most important problems and opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Connect the dots between customer needs, technology capabilities and commercial opportunities to define where Ankar can deliver the greatest impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with stakeholders from hands-on SMEs to senior executives, challenging assumptions and helping customers reimagine what's possible while building excellent rapport and passion for innovation to enable the work that’s needed.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own deployments and drive impact</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead customer engagements from early discovery and pilot scoping through deployment, adoption and expansion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate ambitious, often ambiguous objectives into actionable plans, bringing together customers, engineers, product teams and commercial colleagues to deliver results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Get hands-on with the product, data and customer workflows to solve problems, prototype solutions and unblock progress.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and demonstrate success through measurable customer outcomes, holding the vision of what’s genuinely valuable to the organisation beyond explicit deliverables.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build strategic customer partnerships</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop trusted relationships across complex enterprise organisations, from end users to executive sponsors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify new use cases, stakeholders and opportunities to deepen the impact of Ankar's technology.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with Account Executives to shape account strategy, build compelling business cases and turn successful deployments into broader enterprise partnerships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate complex ideas and results clearly, building conviction and momentum at every level of the organisation.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Help shape the product and how we scale</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a critical bridge between our customers and our product and engineering teams, translating real-world challenges into product insights and opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify patterns across deployments that can inform our product roadmap, new capabilities and future market opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop repeatable approaches, tools and ways of working that help us deliver extraordinary customer outcomes at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help shape the deployment function itself as Ankar grows.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Above all, we're looking for exceptional problem solvers with the curiosity, creativity, judgment and drive to make things happen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You might come from technology, consulting, engineering, product, strategy or an entirely different background. What matters most is how you think, learn and operate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We value:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Intellectual curiosity and analytical rigour. A love for getting to the bottom of complex problems, asking better questions and finding connections others miss.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Value oriented instincts where you naturally look for opportunities to create value, understand what matters to a business, and can connect technical possibilities to meaningful commercial outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Product intuition and technical fluency - excited by technology, comfortable getting hands-on with software and data, and able to work effectively with engineers. You don't need to be a software engineer, but you should be eager and able to learn.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ownership and resourcefulness. A tendency to thrive in ambiguity, take initiative and find ways forward even when there's no established playbook.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communication and empathy. You build trust with people from very different backgrounds, navigate complex stakeholder environments, and can influence and bring people along without formal authority.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Adaptability and low ego - you’ll join a team that is willing to roll up their sleeves at any time and task. We index on value, and care more about outcomes than credit.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A bias for action. You combine big-picture thinking with the willingness and ability to execute.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bonus points:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with enterprise software, AI, data or complex technical products, particularly in customer-facing roles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founding experience, or experience building a new product or business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in R&amp;D-intensive industries such as automotive, semiconductors, advanced materials, chemicals, energy, aerospace or industrial manufacturing, including exposure to complex innovation and product development workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with technical information sources such as scientific literature, patents, experimental results, specifications and research documentation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience prototyping, investigating technical problems or analysing data using Python, SQL, APIs or low-code tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in a fast-paced startup environment.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>The role involves travel, working closely with customers across the US and Europe.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min