&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;*This position is fully remote/home based. Applications will be accepted from candidates based in the UK and the following US states: FL, IL, MA, MD, NY, PA, TX, VA.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Role Summary&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Director, Editorial, you will provide strategic leadership for all editorial functions, setting editorial policies and ensuring the scientific scope, selection criteria, authorship profile, and integrity standards of our journals in support of PLOS&#39;s mission and sustainability. You will be a champion of PLOS’s transformative vision for global, equitable open science while maintaining research integrity standards and contributing sustainably to organizational growth and impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will play a key role in advancing our strategy, enabling the conversion of PLOS&#39;s business model from APCs to institutional and other new revenue models, and evolving our publishing capabilities while ensuring that PLOS’s editorial quality, content integrity and scientific relevance underpin the value of our portfolio and its financial sustainability. You will evolve editorial methods and criteria to meet the challenges of scale and adapt to a rapidly changing research environment, including a focus on the responsible use of AI in research, scholarly communication and publishing. Working closely with colleagues across PLOS, you will ensure that editorial strategy, operational delivery, and business performance are aligned in service of PLOS&#39;s vision for open science.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of PLOS’s senior leadership, you will be part of creating the scholarly communication systems of the future, expanding PLOS&#39;s influence and impact globally. You will champion innovation while ensuring that open science, research integrity, efficiency, and author experience remain at the center of how PLOS operates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A collaborative and mission-driven leader, you will develop high-performing teams, build strong organizational partnerships, and contribute to a culture of transparency, accountability, continuous learning, and shared success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Strategic and Portfolio Leadership&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the portfolio performance by setting well-calibrated editorial criteria that effectively balance quality, mission and sustainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Position PLOS’s journals to be widely recognized in their scientific communities globally, respected as relevant, fair, reliable and innovative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the editorial policies and strategies that enable the transition from an APC-dependent, article-centric model toward an expanded open science offering serving an increasingly diverse community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, implement and communicate the research integrity policies that support a transformation of PLOS’s approach to meet emerging integrity challenges, within the integrity policy framework and risk posture set by the CSO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help evolve the traditional notion of peer-review to address the challenges of scale and respond to changes in technology, research workflows and&amp;nbsp; scholarly communication .&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own day-to-day relationships with Editors-in-Chief and editorial boards in relation to strategic and cross-portfolio matters, keeping them informed and engaged through the transformation and bringing their perspectives into editorial decisions, in partnership with the CSO, who leads PLOS’s senior-level relationships with the scientific community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nurture global, vibrant and performant editorial boards who champion PLOS’s values, by managing the boards composition to support the scope of the portfolio and effectively communicating and upholding consistent editorial, integrity and behavioral standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain awareness of the changing research and scholarly communication environment, including new technologies (including AI), policies, and evolving norms and expectations, to identify new threats and opportunities early and ensure that editorial processes remain appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Operational Leadership&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the performance of editorial operations, partnering with relevant functional leaders to optimize editorial workflows to deliver the editorial strategy, setting and delivering against clear targets for quality, cost of service, and contributor experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish the metrics, reporting and review rhythms that give you, the CSO, and the Executive Team a clear, timely view of editorial and integrity performance across the portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adapt editorial workflows to help deliver the business model transition and new publishing capabilities that expand the open science offering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the department budget and execute against organizational priorities through responsible resource management,&amp;nbsp; sound prioritization, and pro-actively managing capacity and necessary trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with colleagues across functions to anticipate, flag and mitigate risks to standards, revenue or costs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold research integrity policies through your accountability for monitoring operational effectiveness, rapid response to new challenges, management of case handling, and holding day-to-day responsibility for arbitrating case decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold teams, vendors, and volunteers to clear performance standards, intervening early where quality or policy drift occurs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Leadership and Culture&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead a cohesive editorial leadership team with clear roles, shared goals and real accountability to each other and to peers across PLOS. Develop your leaders into strong people leaders through clear expectations, coaching and mentorship, and set and uphold performance and behavioral standards, addressing gaps promptly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own hiring, retention and succession planning across editorial, building a bench capable of stepping into senior roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead editorial teams through the change PLOS’s transformation requires, creating trust, clarity and engagement through visible, accessible leadership, and inspiring change rather than working around resistance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a collaborative leader across PLOS. Own outcomes across functional boundaries, anticipate what peers driving shared priorities need from Editorial, surface issues early and directly with the colleagues involved, and escalate to the CSO when they’re unresolved.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage the scientific and professional expertise of editorial teams, internally and externally, in service of PLOS’s mission. Support their professional development and their visibility in their communities, so they champion PLOS’s transformative mission with a coherent voice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced scientific or medical qualifications, typically a PhD degree with&amp;nbsp; relevant research experience providing strong scientific credibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant, progressively responsible publishing and leadership experience in STM publishing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven record of leading through layers of managers: building leadership teams, developing people leaders, and addressing performance issues directly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated operational strength, including delivering measurable improvements in workflow performance, quality and cost, and owning budgets and vendor relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading teams through significant organizational change.Demonstrated ability to work effectively across cultures, disciplines, and organizational functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of scholarly publishing markets, publishing policies, research integrity, and editorial models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, influencing and leadership skills, with the ability to align diverse stakeholders around shared objectives. .&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong scientific credibility and the ability to build trusted relationships across the research community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business problem solver – operates with curiosity to get to the root of the business problem to ensure the ultimate solution is grounded in organizational strategy and mission.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dedication to open science and transforming scholarly communication, with a genuine interest in engaging productively with the scientific community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading high-volume journal portfolios and/or megajournals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range we’ve established for these positions is (&lt;strong&gt;US): $180,000- $191,000 or (UK) £115,000- £125,000&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;PLOS also offers a comprehensive benefits package summarized below.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;BENEFITS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401k with employer match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee sponsored health, dental and vision insurance (Dental and Vision 100% employer paid)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Vacation, 11 public holidays and sick leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Birthday and three winter holidays days off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Short term and long term disability insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2 days paid time off for volunteering per year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully remote work environment with stipend on joining for home office&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;UK:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Private medical insurance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Life assurance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Income protection &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Personal accident insurance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Pension with up to 10% employer match&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;25 days holidays, market competitive Maternity and Paternity leave&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Birthday and three winter holidays days off&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;2 days paid time off for volunteering per year&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;Fully remote work environment with stipend on joining for home office&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About PLOS&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Building on a strong legacy of pioneering innovation, PLOS continues to be a catalyst in open science, reimagining models to meet open science principles, removing barriers and promoting inclusion in knowledge creation and sharing, and publishing research outputs that enable everyone to learn from, reuse and build upon scientific knowledge.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our work is supported by a highly skilled global in-house team, partnerships with local scholarly organizations, and the valued contributions of a diverse, international community of scientific researchers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re committed to equal opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re working to create a more equitable system of scientific knowledge and understanding. Removing barriers to inclusion and facilitating broad participation of voices is core to our success, inside and out.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond accepting distinct perspectives, we seek and support divergent backgrounds among our staff because we know differences strengthen our teams, our work, and our communities. We strongly encourage applicants of all identities to join us as we work towards a future where science is open to all, for all.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit&lt;a href=&quot;http://plos.org/careers&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;plos.org/careers&lt;/a&gt; to learn more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;To learn more about how PLOS protects your privacy, see our &lt;a href=&quot;https://plos.org/employee-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Employee Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/plos/editorial-director-141491","tags":["Editorial"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1795730119},{"slug":"senior-global-data-solutions-manager-london-400370","company_name":"Zoominfo","title":"Senior Global Data Solutions Manager","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;ZoomInfo is where careers accelerate. We move fast, think boldly, and empower you to do the best work of your life. You’ll be surrounded by teammates who care deeply, challenge each other, and celebrate wins. With tools that amplify your impact and a culture that backs your ambition, you won’t just contribute. You’ll make things happen fast.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;markdown-p&quot;&gt;When an enterprise customer says our data is bad, they are usually wrong about the cause and entirely right about the pain. As our first Senior Global Data Solutions Manager, you will sit inside Core &amp;amp; Global Data, next to the PMs who own company data, person data, matching and hierarchy, and point your expertise outward at our sellers, CSMs and their customers. You bring deep B2B data knowledge and the teaching instinct to share it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;markdown-p&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;markdown-strong&quot;&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;markdown-ul&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;markdown-li&quot;&gt;Own the data conversation with a named book of enterprise customers, embedding for weeks with their admin and systems integrator.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;markdown-li&quot;&gt;Diagnose what is wrong (a data defect, configuration error, wrong endpoint or unset expectation) and show the evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;markdown-li&quot;&gt;Translate a customer&#39;s definition of an account into an implementable hierarchy: what rolls up, what stays distinct, what gets purged, and where ZoomInfo informs versus overrides.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;markdown-li&quot;&gt;Lead the international data conversation, covering coverage by country, registry data and its limits, regional entity and address conventions, and privacy constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;markdown-li&quot;&gt;Set expectations on what our metrics mean, such as what a confidence score blends and what a coverage figure counts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;markdown-li&quot;&gt;Review enrichment thresholds, match settings and field mapping before production against how the customer actually works.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;markdown-li&quot;&gt;Educate our managers, CSMs and AMs through working sessions, office hours and in-channel answers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;markdown-li&quot;&gt;Write answers back into our knowledge tools so repeat questions stop reaching a person.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;markdown-p&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;markdown-strong&quot;&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;markdown-p&quot;&gt;&lt;em class=&quot;markdown-em&quot;&gt;Must-Have&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;markdown-ul&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;markdown-li&quot;&gt;5+ years of deep B2B data expertise as a practitioner with firmographic, contact or identity data. You know what good coverage looks like because you measured it, and how match rate is legitimately calculated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;markdown-li&quot;&gt;Fluency in go-to-market jobs: you understand what a seller, AM, CSM and RevOps lead each need, and reason from their problem inward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;markdown-li&quot;&gt;Customer-facing range and diagnostic honesty: you are credible with a CRM admin debugging a match rule and with an escalated VP, and you neither defend data reflexively nor concede it to keep the peace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;markdown-li&quot;&gt;Working knowledge of how data gets consumed, including CRM data models (Salesforce especially), API-delivered data, enrichment configuration and hierarchy structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;markdown-li&quot;&gt;International experience with non-US company or contact data, and an understanding of where regional differences matter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;markdown-p&quot;&gt;&lt;em class=&quot;markdown-em&quot;&gt;Preferred&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;markdown-ul&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;markdown-li&quot;&gt;A teaching instinct with evidence behind it: you have made others materially better at something technical.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;markdown-li&quot;&gt;Experience on the customer side of a B2B data implementation you personally owned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;markdown-li&quot;&gt;Experience with public business registries such as Companies House or the Nordic registries, or equivalents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;markdown-li&quot;&gt;Experience designing or arguing through an account hierarchy model, including the contentious merge decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;markdown-li&quot;&gt;Built internal education that people kept using after the session ended.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;markdown-p&quot;&gt;#LI-Hybrid #LI-JS1&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;markdown-p&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ZoomInfo (NASDAQ: GTM), the all-in-one AI GTM platform, enables sales, marketing, and customer success teams to execute their go-to-market strategy with confidence. Powered by the industry&#39;s most comprehensive B2B data, including more than 100 million companies, 500 million contacts, and billions of signals, ZoomInfo delivers the intelligence, automation, and integrations that modern revenue teams need to identify, engage, and convert their best buyers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ZoomInfo is committed to protecting your privacy when you apply for jobs with us. Please review our Job Applicant &lt;a href=&quot;https://drive.google.com/file/d/1yiG-k0YX_sW10PiJk_xliDc3W-veJCrK/view?usp=drive_link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; for more details on how we handle your personal information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ZoomInfo may use a software-based assessment as part of the recruitment process. More information about this tool, including the results of the most recent bias audit, is available &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoominfo.com/legal/nyc-local-law-144-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ZoomInfo is proud to be an equal opportunity employer, hiring based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, and does not discriminate based on protected status. We welcome all applicants and are committed to providing equal employment opportunities regardless of sex, race, age, color, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, disability status, religion, protected military or veteran status, medical condition, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. We also consider qualified candidates with criminal histories in accordance with legal requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For Massachusetts Applicants: It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment. An employer who violates this law shall be subject to criminal penalties and civil liability. ZoomInfo does not administer lie detector tests to applicants in any location.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/zoominfo/senior-global-data-solutions-manager-london-400370","tags":["909 Product Management - Data"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1795730117},{"slug":"enterprise-account-executive-london-247195","company_name":"Anaplan","title":"Enterprise Account Executive","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Anaplan, we are a team of innovators focused on optimizing business decision-making through our leading AI-infused scenario planning and analysis platform so our customers can outpace their competition and the market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What unites Anaplanners across teams and geographies is our collective commitment to our customers’ success and to our Winning Culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;Our customers rank among the who’s who in the Fortune 50. Coca-Cola, LinkedIn, Adobe, LVMH and Bayer are just a few of the 2,400+ global companies who rely on our best-in-class platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt; Our Winning Culture is the engine that drives our teams of innovators. We champion diversity of thought and ideas, we behave like leaders regardless of title, we are committed to achieving ambitious goals, and we love celebrating&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;our wins – big and small.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Supported by operating principles of being strategy-led, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anaplan.com/careers/&quot;&gt;values-&lt;/a&gt;based and disciplined in execution, you’ll be inspired, connected, developed and rewarded here. Everything that makes you unique is welcome; join us and let’s build what’s next - together!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anaplan is seeking an &lt;strong&gt;ENTERPRISE ACCOUNT EXECUTIVE&lt;/strong&gt; in London, to drive its growth and expand across the UK within Enterprise&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will take your proven track record of selling sophisticated technology solutions and account management and sell an incredibly versatile platform. Our sales team is helping industry leaders understand the impact of Anaplan products and how our connected planning solution is ending siloed decision-making. You will help our customers achieve their immediate business goals while setting their business up for the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be a catalyst to Anaplan’s continued growth while leading digital transformation. Reporting directly to the RVP of Sales. You will have mostly greenfield accounts. This type of territory requires someone to further build our footprint by hunting and locking in new logo accounts as well as rapidly growing opportunities within the current customer base.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engaging with targeted prospects to identify broken business processes and position Anaplan’s unique ability to solve the problem,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build Anaplan’s business value throughout the selling engagement. Navigating sophisticated prospect environments to align the prospect around the Anaplan solution,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct highly effective presentations from Director through SVP and key C-suite level decision makers including CFOs, CROs, and senior leaders in supply chain, workforce, and other business functions,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop customers and own opportunity management start-to-finish across multiple customer targets and functions,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply Anaplan’s value-based selling methodology and tools to run sales processes and accurately forecast business,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employ outstanding account leadership skills to identify account expansion opportunities by cross-selling and up-selling opportunities within targeted accounts,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform strategic sales planning, leading to accurate forecasting of the business,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with cross-functional members of Sales Development Reps, Marketing, Solution Consultants, and the Customer Success teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience in consultative sales with Enterprise customers, ideally in SaaS solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&#39;Hunter&#39; with a strong growth mindset, motivated by developing new business as well as developing existing large accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in verticals to include Retail, Energy, Manufacturing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of overachieving sales quota &amp;amp; targets, including demonstrated history of multiple high six-figure annual contract value (ACV) deals (services and/or software),&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated network in your industry territory, with a mix of some customers and implementation partners,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience with sophisticated partner &amp;amp; internal team organisations,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain understanding (Supply Chain, FP&amp;amp;A, Workforce Planning &amp;amp; Sales) and knowledge of how these functions plan, process work and make decisions,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong, demonstrated opportunity management practices (e.g. sales process, qualification, executive presentation skills, quote presentation and negotiation), and ability to balance multiple (3-5) opportunities at once,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business, Finance, Economics, related BS/BA degree or relevant years of experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Outreach, SFDC, LinkedIn Sales Navigator a plus,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Account Planning experience Altify, MEDDPICC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity, Equity, Inclusion and Belonging (DEIB) &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe attracting and retaining the best talent and fostering an inclusive culture strengthens our business. DEIB improves our workforce, enhances trust with our partners and customers, and drives business success. Build your career in a place where diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging aren’t just words on paper – this is what drives our innovation, it’s how we connect, and it contributes to what makes us a market leader. We believe in a hiring and working environment where all people are respected and valued, regardless of gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, religion, ethnicity, age, neurodiversity, disability status, citizenship, or any other aspect which makes people unique. We hire you for who you are, and we want you to bring your authentic self to work every day! &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We will ensure that individuals with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodation to participate in the job application or interview process, perform essential job functions, and receive equitable benefits and all privileges of employment. Please contact us to request accommodation. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fraud Recruitment Disclaimer&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It has come to our attention that fraudulent and fictitious job opportunities are being circulated on the Internet. Prospective candidates are being contacted by certain individuals, mainly through telephone calls, emails and correspondence, claiming they are representatives of Anaplan. The main purpose of these correspondences and announcements is to obtain privileged information from individuals.  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anaplan does not: &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extend offers to candidates without an extensive interview process with a member of our recruitment team and a hiring manager via video or in person.  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Send job offers via email. All offers are first extended verbally by a member of our internal recruitment team whenever possible and then followed up via written communication. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All emails from Anaplan would come from an ----- email address. Should you have any doubts about the authenticity of an email, letter or telephone communication purportedly from, for, or on behalf of Anaplan, please send an email to ----- before taking any further action in relation to the correspondence.  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW36347262 BCX0&quot;&gt;Privacy &amp;amp; AI&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW36347262 BCX0&quot;&gt; Notice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW238761408 BCX0&quot;&gt;C&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW238761408 BCX0&quot;&gt;andidate data processed during our recruitment activities is handled &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW238761408 BCX0&quot;&gt;in accordance with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW238761408 BCX0&quot;&gt; our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anaplan.com/legal/candidate-privacy-notice/&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;. This may include the use of artificial intelligence or automated tools to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW238761408 BCX0&quot;&gt;assist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW238761408 BCX0&quot;&gt; our team in evaluating qualifications.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/anaplan/enterprise-account-executive-london-247195","tags":["Field Sales"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1795730116},{"slug":"2028-graduates-intern-antitrust-competition-economics-practice-summer-2027-london-188850","company_name":"charlesriverassociates","title":"[2028 graduates] Intern (Antitrust & Competition Economics Practice) - Summer 2027","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Charles River Associates&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.crai.com/&quot;&gt;Charles River Associates&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; is a leading global consulting firm that offers economic, financial, and strategic expertise to major law firms, corporations, and governments around the world.&amp;nbsp; CRA advises clients on economic and financial matters pertaining to litigation and regulatory proceedings, and guides corporations through critical business strategy and performance-related issues. Since 1965, clients have engaged CRA for its combination of industry experience and rigorous, fact-based analysis that provide clients with clear, implementable solutions to complex business concerns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CRA&#39;s &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ecp.crai.com/&quot;&gt;European Competition practice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; specialises in providing economic advice on matters of competition policy and regulation. We assist firms and their legal advisors in all types of competition proceedings before competition authorities and courts: mergers and acquisitions, abuse of dominance allegations, cartels, restrictive commercial agreements, market investigations, litigation and disputes, intellectual property or state aid. We also provide advice to regulatory authorities in similar matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have played a key role in many cases that have shaped European competition policy in recent years: from aerospace to software, and manufacturing to transportation. More recently, we have been at the forefront of economic thinking in antitrust investigations and regulation in the tech sector.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We seek candidates for our London, UK location.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.crai.com/careers/intern-program/&quot;&gt;Summer Analyst/Associate Internship program&lt;/a&gt; mirrors the analyst experience to give you an understanding of our business and experience project work at Charles River Associates. Throughout the 8-10 week program, Analyst/Associate Interns work alongside senior colleagues to deliver live client consulting projects within the practice area. Along the way, you’ll benefit from professional development and wellness support programs, social events to connect you with peers and a collegial work environment. Successful interns will be offered a full-time position following graduation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Interns work closely with senior consultants, scholars and industry experts on project teams, and will have the opportunity to assist on some of the largest, high-profile and most significant competition cases in Europe. A typical Intern would:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify potential issues and conduct analyses that can be used to illustrate economic arguments;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assemble compelling evidence from data and research that support our expert opinions and business recommendations;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Program, build models and/or perform regression analyses in statistical analysis programs (such as Stata, Python, R), including large data projects requiring use of cloud computing;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in the development and presentation of client deliverables, including expert reports and white papers summarising opinions, conclusions, and recommendations using financial, market, industry or client-proprietary data;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate complicated economic concepts and arguments to internal teams in an understandable, accessible manner;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the integrity and accuracy of analyses and opinions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pursuing an undergraduate degree in economics from well-regarded institutions, graduating between December 2027 and August 2028;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong foundation in microeconomics, industrial economics and/or econometrics;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High degree of numeracy and comfort with data manipulation are essential, familiarity with econometric techniques desirable;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious and analytical thinkers who bring creative approaches to non-standard problems;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective oral and written communication skills;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eagerness to learn new skills and programming languages;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated high level of initiative and leadership;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong teamwork and collaboration capabilities;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent time management and task prioritisation skills; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and demonstrated interest in consulting through coursework, work experience, activities, or attendance at CRA recruiting events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To Apply&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To be considered for this position, please submit the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CV/Resume&lt;/strong&gt; – please include current address, personal email and telephone number;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Covering letter&lt;/strong&gt; – please describe your interest in the European Competition practice and how this role matches your goals.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The internship will take place from Monday 28&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-fontsize=&quot;12&quot;&gt;th&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; June 2027 – Friday 3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-fontsize=&quot;12&quot;&gt;rd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; September 2027.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professional Development&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CRA’s robust &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.crai.com/cra-careers/talent-development/&quot;&gt;skills development programs&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.crai.com/benefits/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;wellness programming&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; encourage you to thrive as an individual and team member. We provide interns a variety of technical training, presentation skills, internal seminars, and performance coaching over the summer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location Flexibility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CRA creates a work environment that enables our colleagues to benefit from being together in the office to best deliver on our promise of career growth, mentorship and inclusivity. At the same time, we recognise that individuals realise a range of benefits when working from home periodically. We currently ask that individuals spend 3 to 4 days a week on average working in the office (which may include traveling to another CRA office or to a client&#39;s location), with specific days determined in coordination with your practice or team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsible AI Use in Recruiting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that recruiting is fundamentally a human process, and we are committed to a hiring process that is consistent, transparent, and people-focused. While AI and other technology-enabled tools help our team operate more efficiently, we strive to provide every candidate with a personalized, thoughtful, and high-touch experience. As CRA invests significant human effort to find qualified members for our teams, we expect candidates to invest corresponding human effort to learn about CRA, prepare thoughtful application materials, and engage with our interviewers. Read more about appropriate hiring manager, recruiting team, and candidate AI at CRA &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.crai.com/cra-careers/ai-recruiting/&quot;&gt;on our website&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Charles River Associates is an equal opportunity employer (Equality Act 2010). As part of our focus on equity and inclusion, we work to ensure a fair and consistent hiring process. We celebrate diversity and we are committed to an inclusive work environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;The statements included in this job description are intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by people assigned to this job.&amp;nbsp; They are not intended to be an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties and skills required of personnel so classified.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/charlesriverassociates/2028-graduates-intern-antitrust-competition-economics-practice-summer-2027-london-188850","tags":["Antitrust & Competition Economics"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1795730115},{"slug":"commercial-relations-manager-eu-uk-london-442729","company_name":"Scarlet","title":"Commercial Relations Manager – EU & UK","description":"<h2><strong>We pull medical technology from the future to solve human health.</strong></h2><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scarlet is authorised to assess and certify medical devices. We combine clinical, technical and regulatory expertise with AI agents and software so rigorous certification can keep pace with product development at the world’s most ambitious technology companies, without lowering the safety bar.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our customers have cut a year or more from their certification timelines for new AI-enabled medical devices and shortened product-update cycles from months to weeks. You’ll join a team building the infrastructure that makes these outcomes repeatable at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who you are</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have strong experience of developing a productive professional network in a new industry, and great relationships with key stakeholders within it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You understand the importance of providing an exceptional experience when connecting and working with those stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re insatiably curious about the world and what makes people tick</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a high EQ, hugely enjoy meeting new people, and can easily navigate complex human relationships</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can build rapport with people across the industry: from senior figures at established firms to one-person consultancies, and everyone in between</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have outstanding written &amp; verbal communication skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You balance thorough reflection with action; you think deeply and operate at pace</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Desirable</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a well-developed network in, and knowledge of, the European digital health industry</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are keen to travel up to 20% of the time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are familiar with medical device regulation and Software as a Medical Device</p></li></ul><h2><strong><br />What the job involves</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your goal will be to build strong relationships with key third parties in our industry – such as regulatory consultants, lawyers, eQMS providers, and more – such that they advocate for Scarlet and recommend us to their clients. In practice this means building both knowledge <em>(so they understand who we are and what makes us different)</em> and trust (<em>so they are confident in working with us)</em>. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Details:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build deep connections with individuals and organisations in Scarlet’s ecosystem</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Furnish these connections with the required knowledge and material to understand Scarlet and the value we offer to healthcare innovators</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate closely with the broader Marketing and Commercial team to effectively communicate Scarlet’s mission and value proposition to the key third parties in our industry</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure those third parties wish to recommend Scarlet to their clients and connections, and have an exceptional, world-class experience when dealing with us</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Attend industry events to grow awareness and adoption of Scarlet</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Iterate our Commercial Relations processes to align with Scarlet’s ambitious commercial goals</p></li></ul><h2><strong><br />The interview process </strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">(we will likely collapse 2/3 later-stage interviews into one in-person session)</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Intro call with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/amnon-ferber/">Amnon</a> - 20 mins</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interview with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/amnon-ferber/">Amnon</a> - 45 mins</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interview with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/karanfarora/">Karan</a> - 30 mins</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Case interview with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/danlevy1/"><u>Dan</u></a> - 45 mins</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interview with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/james-dewar-78758992/"><u>James</u></a> - 20 mins</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interview with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jamie-cox-01458b3a/"><u>Jamie</u></a> - 20 mins</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Referencing</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offer</p></li></ol><hr><p>Compensation: £90K – £110K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • £90K – £110K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/scarlet/commercial-relations-manager-eu-uk-london-442729","tags":["Growth"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"UK - London Office","created_at":1795729212},{"slug":"growth-uk-293534","company_name":"Kyra","title":"Growth","description":"<h2><strong>About Kyra</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Kyra is an enterprise influencer marketing platform working with brands like SharkNinja, Coach, H&amp;M, Ray-Ban, and Converse. Our platform manages the full lifecycle — creator discovery, campaign management, content review, payments, analytics, and AI-powered intelligence across TikTok, Instagram, and YouTube.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>💼 The role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll own our events from the first idea to the meetings that come out of them. One month that’s a 15-person dinner in Shoreditch, the next it’s a week at Cannes Lions. 🎬 Either way you write the brief, book the venue, fill the room with the right people from our Top 200 and our partners, and make sure every guest turns up and hears from us afterwards.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The phone is how you make that work. 📞 You’ll call guest lists rather than cold lists, to get people into the room and to follow up once they’ve been. Alongside events you’ll look after our partners, run the partner newsletter and build your own voice on LinkedIn. We’ll measure you on two things: the sales-accepted leads (SALs) you create for our AEs, and the feedback on our events. 📈</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🛠️ What you’ll do</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everything you do hangs off two groups of people: those coming to our events, and our partners. You won’t run cold outbound sequences; those sit with our AEs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🎉 Events, from brief to follow-up</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take each opportunity we spot and make it live: write the brief, book the venue, build the Luma page and description, and start the invites</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build guest lists from the Top 200 and our partners for dinners, breakfasts and conference moments in London, New York and LA</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and run the cadence from invite to the room, so that people arrive, they’re greeted and introduced to the right AE, and they’re followed up the next day</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collect feedback from guests, partners and AEs after every event, and use it to make the next one better</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Travel a lot next year for events and conferences, including the US ✈️</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>📞 Calling and meetings</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Call the guest list before every event: confirm registrants, turn maybes into yeses and chase no-shows</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Call everyone who came within 48 hours, while the conversation is still warm</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Book meetings for our AEs off the back of events and partner intros, with a clear handover: who they are, what they care about, how we met them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep HubSpot clean so every event and partner lead can be traced to a meeting</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🤝 Partners and newsletter</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write and send the partner newsletter: what’s coming up, which brands we’re trying to meet and where partners can help</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own regular touch-bases with our Friends of Kyra partners: onboarding them, keeping them close to our events, and logging their intros and referrals</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>📣 Social and your own brand</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build your own presence on LinkedIn. We’re pushing hard on social across Kyra and you’ll be one of its voices</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn every event into content: what got said in the room, not just who came</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🔍 Who we’re looking for</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>✅ Must-haves</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2–4 years in events, partnerships, community or an SDR role, ideally dealing with senior people at brands</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You love the phone, and would rather call than send a third email ☎️</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ve run events people talked about afterwards, and you sweat the details: the seating plan, the intro, the follow-up</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You post on LinkedIn already, or badly want to</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You use Claude every day to research guests, write invites, plan events and build your own workflows 🤖</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re up for a lot of travel next year, including the US</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>⭐ Nice-to-haves</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A feel for the creator economy, social and the brands people talk about</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with HubSpot, Luma or beehiiv</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Has built their own Claude skills or automations</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🎁 What you get</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🥂 The rooms. </strong>You’ll sit at the table with CMOs and creator leaders most people at your level only get to email</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🌎 The travel. </strong>New York, LA and the conference circuit next year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🔑 Ownership early. </strong>You’re the second hire on a new team, the events calendar is yours, and the role grows as the team does</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>💡 Help building your own brand. </strong>We run LinkedIn workshops with creators and will work on your posts with you</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🚪 Access. </strong>You’ll work day to day with the Growth team, our AEs and our CEO</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits</strong><br />🌎 Remote-first, so you can work from wherever you do your best work<br />🌴 25 days PTO + bank holidays, 3 wellness days and paid sick leave<br />📚 Annual Learning and Development budget<br />💰 Annual bonus scheme to recognise great work<br />🩺 Healthcare coverage for US-based team members</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI is core to how we operate. Use it to elevate your work. But everything in your application should reflect your own judgement and experience.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">👀 Haven't found your role yet? Join <strong>People of Influence</strong> 🌟</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">📬 We share the best roles in influence every week, and our own jobs go there first 🚀</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🔔 Get notified <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://peopleofinfluence.beehiiv.com/subscribe">here</a> 👈</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>💟 Support</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you have a condition or require an adjustment to our interview process - please let us know so we can make adjustments to support you. Please note that when you submit an application or resume, your data will be processed in line with our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.bamboohr.com/legal/privacy-policy"><strong>privacy policy</strong></a>.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/kyra/growth-uk-293534","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"UK","created_at":1795729212},{"slug":"senior-sales-senior-account-executive-french-speaker-paris-13825","company_name":"Lemlist","title":"Senior Sales / Senior Account Executive - French speaker","description":"<h2>About lemlist</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">lemlist is the AI-powered sales engagement platform helping sales teams build pipeline smarter, not harder.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bootstrapped from day one, we’ve grown from 0 to $50M+ ARR in 8 years without raising a single dollar. Today, 40,000+ sales teams use lemlist to book more meetings and close more deals.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re building the next generation of outbound: AI-first, multi-channel, highly personalized, and deeply integrated into the way modern sales teams work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">And we’re just getting started.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a french native speaker who will be mostly focusing on the French market that said english fluency is mandatory as this is our working language.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Please read carefully and only apply if you speak French fluently</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mission</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your mission is to acquire high-quality customers for lemlist - our Sales Engagement Platform - and, more generally, lemlist's product.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be in charge of the full sales cycle, including prospection, negotiation, the closing phase, and even customer onboarding.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will focus on companies with 200 to 10,000 employees in various industries and sales teams between 5 to 100 people in various industries.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll be both leveraging Inbound (Demo Requests and Product-Led Sales teams) and Outbound (using lemlist to find prospects) - "eat your own dog's food"</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Results</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>After 3 months, you will have</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Show you can follow the process and well manage high quality inbound lead</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shown you are capable of building an outbound pipeline and closing some higher velocity deals (5-10 seats)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Closed some Inbound / Product-Led-Sales customers</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Overall, generated some revenue</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>After 12 months, you will have</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Achieved quotas for most months</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Became an expert with the product</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build relationships with multiple customers, using referrals as a lever to acquire more customers</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Skills</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in French &amp; English</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">4+ Years of experience in a Sales role with closing and are a top performer (top 20%)</p><p style="min-h