uct strategy with the founders, from what we bet on next to what we stop doing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the roadmap end to end</strong>: turn strategy into a living, prioritized roadmap, and decide what we don't build so the team stays on the highest-impact work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run discovery</strong>: spend real time with brands, partners and the field, find the problems worth solving, and validate before we build.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ship with the team</strong>: work shoulder-to-shoulder with engineering and design to scope, prototype, and ship weekly, not quarterly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own launches and outcomes</strong>: drive rollout, watch the data, onboard the business teams, and judge your work by what it moved, not by what shipped.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build the product function itself</strong>: the rituals, the prioritization, the feedback loop from the field.</p></li></ul><h2>What we're looking for</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>3 to 8 years in product</strong>, at least part of it at a startup or scale-up, ideally as an early or first PM. You've taken something from a vague problem to a shipped, used feature, and owned its results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A <strong>generalist</strong> comfortable owning the messy middle: discovery one hour, scoping with engineers the next, writing the launch note after that.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A <strong>bias for action</strong>: you make calls with incomplete data, ship, and iterate from what real users do.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer obsession</strong> that shows up in your decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI-native</strong>: you already build with tools like Claude, Cursor, v0 or Lovable to prototype, research, synthesize, and move the roadmap faster.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to <strong>learn a lot, fast</strong>, in a deep and complex environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fluent French</strong> and professional English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in Paris, with the team at the office (up to 1 day remote per week).</p></li></ul><h3>Bonus</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've built in <strong>e-commerce, marketplaces, adtech, or AI/agent products</strong>, or you're genuinely fascinated by agentic commerce.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A <strong>technical background</strong> (ex-software engineer or CS), so you can go deep with the team and direct AI tools effectively.</p></li></ul><h2>Why join us</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join a company in <strong>early breakout mode</strong>, already generating revenue with a clear edge.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be part of the <strong>next structural shift of the web</strong>: agentic commerce.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work directly with experienced, ambitious founders, and own the product from day one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape both the product <em>and</em> how we build it.</p></li></ul><h2>What we offer</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary, based on experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equity (BSPCE)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meal vouchers with Swile</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Alan health insurance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7 weeks of vacation (RTT included)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">50% transportation coverage</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/lemrock/founding-product-manager-paris-449894","tags":["Product"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"P