e individuals and companies to securely buy, store, swap, grow and manage crypto assets – including the Ledger hardware wallets line with more than 7.5 millions units already sold in 200 countries.	</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The team</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To sustain the company's growth, Ledger is looking for a <strong>Senior Scala Backend Engineer</strong> to join the <strong>Cloud Wallet team</strong>. This team builds and operates the backend services that power blockchain account management, transaction processing and on-chain data aggregation across all Ledger wallet surfaces, from Ledger Live to Ledger Enterprise, the custody platform used by financial institutions. Every client transaction goes through these services, and so does every new blockchain Ledger supports. We believe in the power of functional programming to build robust and scalable platforms. We take time to share, challenge, and grow together through bi-weekly knowledge-sharing sessions, meetups, conferences, and open source contributions.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll be doing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design, build and operate the Scala services that connect Ledger wallets and the Ledger Enterprise platform to blockchain backends: account creation, operation history, transaction crafting, broadcast and lifecycle tracking.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead new blockchain integrations end to end, from the integration design (ADR) to production, across account-based, UTXO and privacy-preserving chains.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own production quality on your scope: SLIs and SLOs, observability, distributed tracing. Take part in the firefighting rotation and drive incidents to resolution, including those raised by institutional clients.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define clear contracts with the Coin Integration and Ledger Enterprise teams, for example where UTXO selection lives or how transaction states are exposed to consumers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write and review ADRs, challenge designs, and raise the bar on code quality, testing (including end-to-end on testnets) and technical debt management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work in an AI-native way: use coding agents daily, write the specifications, constraints and verification that let them deliver safely, and contribute to the team's AI tooling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mentor other engineers and share your knowledge across the Backend Blockchain community.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You will collaborate cross-functionally with:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Coin Integration team for coin modules and new blockchain integrations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Ledger Enterprise team, main consumer of the team's services for institutional custody.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Ledger Wallet, Ledger Button and Wallet XP teams as consumers of the team's backend APIs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Blockchain platform team for data model alignment, indexing and event streaming.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Infrastructure and SRE teams for deployment, reliability and scalability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Security team (Donjon) for vulnerability analysis and remediation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Product team for roadmap prioritization and customer-driven requirements.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-he