bute to the continuous evolution of the embedded platform, including MCU based solutions as well as optional Linux and Yocto based components</p></li><li><p>Develop pragmatic testing strategies to ensure the functionality, reliability, and quality of both hardware and firmware</p></li><li><p>Support development and manufacturing partners with debugging, technical documentation, and production ramp up</p></li><li><p>Provide Level 3 technical support for complex system, firmware, and hardware related issues</p></li><li><p>Travel approximately 5 to 10 percent to support development partners, product validation activities, and product launches</p></li></ul> <br> <ul><li><p class="PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer">Bachelor's or Master's degree in Electrical Engineering, Embedded Systems, Computer Science, or a related discipline, or equivalent practical experience</p></li><li><p>Several years of hands on experience in embedded development, including firmware development and hardware related engineering</p></li><li><p>Strong understanding of hardware design and PCB layouts, with the ability to review design decisions and collaborate effectively with hardware development teams</p></li><li><p>Strong expertise in embedded firmware development and software architecture for microcontroller platforms such as ARM Cortex, ESP32, or STM32</p></li><li><p>Experience with sensor integration and wireless communication technologies such as BLE and WiFi</p></li><li><p>Experience with embedded Linux systems, particularly Yocto, is an advantage, especially in environments combining System on Modules with MCU based architectures</p></li><li><p>Broad system level understanding of mechanics, sensors, actuators, and their integration into robust IoT products</p></li><li><p>Hands on experience with hardware testing, debugging tools, and automated production testing</p></li><li><p>Familiarity with certification standards such as CE and FCC is an advantage</p></li><li><p>Fluent in German and English, with additional languages considered a plus</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/swisspeak-partners-gmbh/iot-embedded-systems-engineer-bern-120533","tags":["Infrastructure & DevOps"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Bern, Berne, Switzerland","created_at":1795739493},{"slug":"consultant-in-public-sector-zurich-414006","company_name":"SwissPeak Partners GmbH","title":"Consultant in Public Sector","description":"<h3 class="PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer"><strong>Your Responsibilities:</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Providing holistic consulting and support for challenging IT client projects</p></li><li><p>Analyzing, optimizing, and digitalizing business processes</p></li><li><p>Creating well-founded business concepts, detailed specifications, and studies</p></li><li><p>Taking responsibility for project management as well as functional and leadership roles within digitalization projects</p></li><li><p>Actively contributing to the growth and further development of the company</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <h3 class="PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer"><strong>Your Profile:</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Completed university degree (University of Applied Sciences, ETH, university) in Business Informatics, Computer Science, Natural Sciences, or a comparable field</p></li><li><p>Strong organizational skills and enthusiasm for conceptual work</p></li><li><p>Entrepreneurial mindset, high level of personal responsibility, and strong communication skills</p></li><li><p>Native-level German required</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/swisspeak-partners-gmbh/consultant-in-public-sector-zurich-414006","tags":["Projectlead 