s and high magnetic fields.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Quality: </strong>Ensure results are traceable, well documented and reproducible.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHO YOU ARE</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">An engineer or scientist who enjoys careful, hands-on experimental work as much as planning how we test at scale.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You hold an MSc or PhD in Physics, Materials Science, Electrical Engineering, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have hands-on experience characterising materials or devices, and are comfortable designing experiments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You speak fluent English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have strong data analysis skills and a solid grasp of measurement uncertainty and statistics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are happy to travel for test campaigns at external facilities, including internationally.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>NICE TO HAVE </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with superconductors, cryogenics or high magnetic fields.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with quality control or production testing at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing cryogenic or automated test equipment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with HTS tape manufacturing processes and the supplier landscape.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">German language skills.<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>This role will initially be based in our Zurich office. As the project develops, the position may move to Germany. If that happens, we’ll give you at least six months’ notice and support you through the move.</strong><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>INTERVIEW PROCESS</strong></p><ul sty