 Marketing team to turn customer needs and business priorities into useful, measurable programs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ideal candidate is both a strategic planner and a hands-on operator. You can build trust with customers, coordinate complex projects across teams and markets, use data to improve programs, and make it straightforward for customers to participate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you will do</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>Customer lifecycle marketing</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan and execute customer marketing programs across onboarding, activation, adoption, engagement, retention, renewal support, and expansion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define customer segments, lifecycle stages, journey maps, messaging, and campaign playbooks that can be adapted for EMEA audiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Customer Success and Customer Enablement to promote onboarding, education, product engagement, and other programs that help customers achieve meaningful outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop proactive re-engagement programs for at-risk or under-engaged accounts using customer health, product usage, support, engagement, and renewal signals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create signal-based campaigns tied to customer needs, product usage, account changes, renewal timing, and expansion fit. Route qualified opportunities to the appropriate Customer Success Managers and account executives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Product Marketing and Product to translate customer feedback into product communications, release messaging, educational content, and lifecycle campaigns.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equip Sales and Customer Success with customer-centric messaging, adoption resources, executive business review materials, playbooks, and clear follow-up paths.</p></li></ul><h3>Customer advocacy and proof</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain a pipeline of EMEA customer advocates based on customer outcomes, engagement, use cases, and willingness to participate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Customer Success Managers and account teams to identify customers for case studies, video testimonials, customer quotes, social content, references, and events.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage customer participation from outreach through briefing, approvals, production, publication, and follow-up. Coordinate logo rights, quotes, and other customer permissions with the appropriate internal teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create and manage a practical customer reference program that supports sales opportunities, renewals, expansions, and strategic marketing needs. Maintain an organized reference pool and manage requests from intake and matching through scheduling, follow-up, and recognition.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own day-to-day Peerbound administration and adoption, including customer profiles, advocacy requests, reference activity, permissions, and reporting. Help Marketing, Sales, and Customer Success use the platform consistently and make fuller use of its capabilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and execute a focused third-party review strategy across relevant platforms, such as G2 and Gartner Peer Insights. Coordinate authentic customer outreach and track review volume, ratings, sentiment, category placement, competitor positioning, and progress against award criteria.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain a qualified pipeline of customer speakers for webinars, user groups, events, panels, and other marketing programs. Confirm speakers early enough to include them in event promotions, landing pages, emails, and social campaigns, and manage briefing, preparation, logistics, approvals, and follow-up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the customer invitation process for Customer Advisory Board opportunities and support customer recruitment for analyst interviews, research, awards, and other strategic initiatives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with Content, Product Marketing, Social, Events, Communications, Analyst Relations, and Creative to elevate customers alongside the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Horizon3.ai">Horizon3.ai</a> brand and turn customer outcomes into reusable marketing assets.</p></li></ul><h3>Program operations and measurement</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build annual and quarterly customer marketing plans for EMEA, manage budgets and resources, and lead cross-functional execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with Marketing Operations, Revenue Operations, and Customer Success Operations to improve segmentation, data quality, trigger detection, nurture, automation, attribution, and reporting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish dashboards and operating rhythms that connect program engagement to adoption, customer advocacy, renewal health, retention, expansion pipeline, and influenced revenue.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define success measures, analyze results, identify opportunities to improve, and iterate on program strategy, messaging, and execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate timelines, owners, status, risks, and next steps clearly across teams. Create practical templates, trackers, and workflows that make customer marketing easier to execute and scale.</p></li></ul><h2>What you bring</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7+ years of marketing experience, including 3+ years in customer marketing, lifecycle marketing, customer advocacy, customer success enablement, or a related discipline.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building customer journeys and programs across adoption, engagement, retention, renewal, expansion, or advocacy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of managing customer stories, references, reviews, speakers, or other advocacy programs, ideally alongside lifecycle marketing responsibilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong relationship-building skills and confidence communicating with customers and internal stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience partnering with Customer Success, Sales, Product Marketing, Product, Marketing Operations, and Revenue Operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong project management and follow-through, with the ability to manage multiple programs and deadlines across teams and markets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analytical and operational skills, including the ability to connect customer behavior and program performance to business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong written and verbal communication skills and the judgment to represent customer perspectives accurately and authentically.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with customer advocacy, reference, review, CRM, or marketing automation platforms. Peerbound experience is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding of B2B SaaS or cybersecurity customer environments is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to work effectively across EMEA markets and time zones. Additional language skills are a plus.</p></li></ul><h2>How success is measured</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lifecycle program engagement and contribution to customer adoption, retention, renewal health, and expansion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Growth and health of the EMEA customer advocate and reference pool, including references fulfilled and customer participation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Customer proof produced, including case studies, videos, quotes, approved logos, and social or event participation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Customer speakers confirmed in time to support event and webinar promotion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Peerbound adoption, data quality, and program activity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review volume, ratings, sentiment, and progress against award criteria.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Customer experience and internal stakeholder satisfaction.</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/horizon3ai/customer-marketing-manager-emea-amsterdam-385802","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam, Netherlands","created_at":1795686017},{"slug":"elektromonteur-senior-uitgeest-118563","company_name":"VDK Groep B.V.","title":"Elektromonteur (Senior)","description":"<p class="MsoNormal">Bij PromTeg doen we wat we beloven. Geen gedoe, wel strak werk waar je trots op bent.</p><p>Je komt terecht in een hechte organisatie van ongeveer 30 collega's waar de lijnen kort zijn en vertrouwen vanzelfsprekend is. Vanuit Uitgeest en Duiven werken we aan multidisciplinaire projecten, service en onderhoud voor grote opdrachtgevers door heel Nederland.</p><p>Hier ben je geen nummer, maar een ervaren vakman die verantwoordelijkheid neemt, collega's verder helpt en een belangrijke rol speelt binnen technische projecten. Je krijgt veel vrijheid in je werk en kunt rekenen op een team dat achter je staat.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Als <strong>Elektromonteur (Senior)</strong> werk je aan complexe installaties binnen de utiliteit. Je combineert elektrotechnische werkzaamheden met andere technische disciplines en bent een technisch aanspreekpunt voor collega's, projectleiding en klanten op locatie.</p><h3>Wat wij je bieden</h3><ul><l