escription":"<p class="MsoNormal"><em>Je installeert en onderhoudt beveiligingssystemen zoals camera’s en toegangscontrole. Op locatie pak jij de leiding: je stuurt collega’s aan, houdt overzicht en zorgt dat het werk goed en op tijd wordt opgeleverd!</em></p><p class="MsoNormal">Onze Hoofd Monteur Beveiligingstechniek schakelt met klanten en je collega’s van kantoor, denkt mee in oplossingen en zorgt dat systemen optimaal draaien.</p><p class="MsoNormal">Je vertrekt grotendeels van huis uit en werkt in schone omgevingen.</p><p class="MsoNormal">Word jij gelukkig van projecten in de kost? Soms hebben wij projecten met een grote reisafstand. Als Hoofd Monteur Beveiligingstechniek werk je dan 4 dagen op locatie en ben je de 5de dag vrij.</p><p class="MsoNormal"> </p><h3>Wat wij je bieden</h3><ul><li><p>Een sterk arbeidsvoorwaardenpakket dat past bij een ervaren monteur met verantwoordelijkheid! </p></li><li><p>25 vakantiedagen en 13 ADV-dagen</p></li><li><p>Goede pensioenregeling (Pensioenopbouw via PMT)</p></li><li><p>Product trainingen via leveranciers om je kennis te vergroten</p></li><li><p>Passend vervoer, laptop en een netto telefoonvergoeding van € 50,- per maand</p></li><li><p>Inspirerende teamuitjes, vrijdagmiddagborrels en een jaarlijks familiefeest (Phantasialand in 2026)</p></li><li><p>Toegang tot de diverse VDK Groep voordelen met kortingen op verzekeringen, verzekeringen, brandstof, attracties, bekende merken, fietsregeling en nog veel meer!&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>Indien interesse in incidentele projecten in de kost;</p><ul><li><p>Je werkt 4 dagen in de kost op locatie in Duitsland of België</p></li><li><p>Je bent vrij op de 5de dag (vrijdag)</p></li><li><p>Hotel en eten wordt verzorgd</p></li><li><p>Je ontvangt een bruto overnachtingsvergoeding van € 100,-</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><h3>Wat ga je doen</h3><p class="MsoNormal">Als Senior Monteur Beveiligingstechniek werk je aan uiteenlopende projecten. Je installeert, begeleid en draagt zorg aan systemen om betrouwbaar en toekomstbestendig te blijven.</p><ul><li><p>Uitvoeren en coördineren van beveiligingsprojecten (CCTV, toegangscontrole en inbraak)</p></li><li><p>Bewaken van de voortgang van project en afstemmen met opdrachtgevers</p></li><li><p>Onderhouden van contact en samenwerking met opdrachtgevers, leveranciers en collega’s</p></li><li><p>Coachen en begeleiden van collega’s op locatie</p></li><li><p>Verantwoordelijk voor de volledige installatieprojecten op locatie.</p></li><li><p>Signaleren en doorvoeren van verbeteringen</p></li><li><p>Uitvoeren van preventief en periodiek onderhoud</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p><h3>&nbsp;Wat neem je mee</h3><ul><li><p>Opleiding in elektrotechniek of vergelijkbaar</p></li><li><p>Ervaring in beveiligingstechniek is een pré</p></li><li><p>Leidinggevende kwaliteiten en overzicht houden op projecten</p></li><li><p>Technisch inzicht en probleemoplossend vermogen</p></li><li><p>Proactieve houding en initiatief</p></li><li><p>Goede communicatieve vaardigheden</p></li><li><p>Goede beheersing van de Nederlandse taal.</p></li><li><p>Rijbewijs B en Verklaring van Betrouwbaarheid</p></li></ul><p>Dus heb je al ervaring als hoofd monteur, eerste monteur, teamleider, meewerkend voorman, of Leidinggevend monteur? </p><p>Dan staat de koffie klaar!</p><p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p><h3>Highlights</h3><ul><li><p>Standplaats: Assendelft, Noord-Holland,&nbsp;Nederland</p></li><li><p>Regio: Projecten Landelijk (vertrekkend van huis, rekening houdend met jouw woonplaats) Incidenteel in Duitsland en België.</p></li><li><p>Team: technisch team met monteurs en projectleiding</p></li><li><p>Projecttype: beveiligingssystemen binnen diverse omgevingen</p></li><li><p>Werkomgeving: Schoon, professioneel, innovatief en oplossingsgericht</p></li></ul><h3>&nbsp;</h3><h3>Shield Beveiligingstechniek &amp; VDK Groep</h3><p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;Shield Beveiligingstechniek is specialist in beveiligingsoplossingen en werkt aan projecten waarbij kwaliteit, betrouwbaarheid en innovatie centraal staan. Je werkt met moderne technieken en systemen op verschillende locaties in schone omgevingen waar initiatief en vakmanschap worden gewaardeerd. Het is een platte organisatie met weinig personeelsverloop.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">Wij zijn een trots onderdeel van de snelgroeiende VDK Groep, maar opereren met een eigen identiteit en cultuur. Je voelt je thuis bij Shield Beveiligingstechniek, terwijl je kunt bouwen op de kracht van de VDK Groep. Dit betekent; Extra voordelen zoals stabiliteit, volop opleidingskansen, doorgroeimogelijkheden en veel extra secundaire arbeidsvoorwaarden! De VDK Groep is medio April 2026 zo’n 180 bedrijven en ruim 7000 medewerkers groot en gevestigd in 6 Europese landen.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>Contact</h3><p class="MsoNormal">Heb je interesse?<br>Mail, bel of app dan met;</p><p class="MsoNormal">Nadine Verhage</p><p class="MsoNormal">Recruitment Business Partner Shield Beveiliging</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">Telefoon: 06-44871851<br>Email:&nbsp;<a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">#LI-NV1</p><p>#VDKGROEPBeveiligingstechniek</p> <br> <h3></h3><p class="MsoNoSpacing">&nbsp;</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/vdk-groep-bv/remote-hoofd-monteur-beveiligingstechniek-datacenters-midden-nederland-assendelft-101384","tags":["Monteur","Remote"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Werken op afstand","created_at":1795685485},{"slug":"junior-business-controller-data-specialist-almere-394785","company_name":"HG International b.v.","title":"Junior Business Controller (Data specialist)","description":"<p class="MsoNormal">Do you enjoy working with numbers, analysing data and finding out what is really happening behind the figures? As Junior Business Controller at HG, you will support our Controllers and Group Financial Controller with financial analyses, reporting and increasingly data-driven insights.</p><p class="MsoNormal">At HG, you will work in a compact organisation with an international reach. You will get the opportunity to learn from experienced colleagues, take responsibility early and turn financial and business data into insights that help us make better decisions. We value people who are curious, take initiative and have the energy to turn ideas into action.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">As Junior Business Controller, you will support our Controllers and gradually build your own areas of responsibility. The role combines financial activities with a strong focus on data, analysis and improving management information.</p><p class="MsoNormal">You will:</p><ul><li><p>support the Business Controllers with financial analyses, reporting and recurring control activities;</p></li><li><p>own and maintain the data model</p></li><li><p>analyse financial and business data and translate it into useful insights;</p></li><li><p>investigate differences, trends and developments and help explain what is happening behind the numbers;</p></li><li><p>build, review and improve data models used for reporting and analysis;</p></li><li><p>use various tools including Excel and Power BI to make information clearer and easier to use;</p></li><li><p>investigate how data flows from source to report and identify opportunities to improve data quality and reporting;</p></li><li><p>help reduce manual work by finding smarter and more reliable ways of working;</p></li><li><p>contribute to improvements in management information and financial processes;</p></li><li><p>translate questions from colleagues into practical analyses and insights.</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal">An important part of the role is conceptual thinking about data. You understand how information should be structured, see connections between different data points and can think about how a data model can be improved to provide better business insights.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Your development in data</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Next to your finance responsibilities, you will grow step by step into the data side of the role, coached by our current Data Specialist. You do not need to master these areas from day one: together we will set up a development path in which you learn to:</p><ul><li><p>contribute to HG's Business Intelligence and data strategy, making sure data supports our company goals;</p></li><li><p>design and maintain data models (such as star schemas) and database/Lakehouse structures, so that data is accurate, reliable and accessible;</p></li><li><p>integrate data from different sources and systems in a medallion model (Bronze for raw data, Silver for engineering, Gold for consumption);</p></li><li><p>manage the HG Data Dictionary, data repositories and the underlying data architecture;</p></li><li><p>apply data governance and data quality practices, including audit trails, data privacy requirements and best-practice frameworks such as DAMA;</p></li><li><p>map business processes (BPMN 2.0) and translate business requirements into practical data solutions;</p></li><li><p>work with tools such as SQL, Python (pandas), Power Query, Power Automate and Microsoft Fabric, and over time explore AI techniques;</p></li><li><p>document data models and data processes, and monitor data systems for performance and reliability.</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal">This gives you a strong combination of finance and data expertise, which is becoming increasingly valuable in modern Business Control.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Collaboration &amp; positioning</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">You will be part of the Finance team and work closely with our Business Controllers. This gives you the opportunity to learn from experienced colleagues while contributing your own analytical and data-driven perspective.</p><p class="MsoNormal">Because HG is a relatively compact organisation, you will have direct contact with colleagues across different disciplines. This means you can quickly see how your analyses and improvements are being used in the business. At the same time, you will work within an international organisation, with colleagues and markets across Europe.</p><p class="MsoNormal">The role is based at our head office in Almere.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>HG is a compact, fast-growing and international organization where you can directly see the impact of your work. This requires ownership, initiative and a pragmatic, results-oriented mindset. The team culture is open, pragmatic and focused on results, encouraging you to bring ideas forward, challenge constructively and take responsibility. Everything we do is guided by our three core values: Aim High, Be Brave, Be Connected.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p class="MsoNormal"><strong>What you bring</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">We are looking for someone who is analytical, energetic and curious. You enjoy getting to the bottom of a question rather than simply producing a report. You want to understand why the numbers look the way they do and how the underlying data can provide better insights.</p><p class="MsoNormal">You bring:</p><ul><li><p>willingness to learn</p></li><li><p>around 3–5 years of relevant work experience, for example as a big 4 auditor, Finance Analyst, Data Analyst or Junior Business Controller;</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraph">solid knowledge of finance and accounting, preferably gained through an education in Accountancy, Finance &amp; Control, Business Information Management, Data Analytics);</p></li><li><p>experience with or a strong interest in Power BI;</p></li><li><p>strong analytical skills;</p></li><li><p>the ability to think conceptually about data, reporting and data models;</p></li><li><p>a curious and proactive approach to solving problems;</p></li><li><p>the confidence to ask questions and challenge existing ways of working;</p></li><li><p>an energetic mindset and the drive to learn and improve;</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraph">a genuine eagerness to learn and to keep developing yourself, both in finance and in data;</p></li><li><p>fluent English; knowledge of Dutch is desirable.</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW38523178 BCX8">experience with AI tools, such as Copilot.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><em>Please note that we do not offer visa or work permit sponsorship for this position. You must therefore hold a valid EU work permit</em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>What we offer</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">This is a role where you can build a strong foundation in modern Business Control while developing further in data and analytics. You will not only work with existing reports and figures, but also have the opportunity to improve how information is structured, analysed and used.</p><p class="MsoNormal">You can expect:</p><ul><li><p class="MsoNormal">a monthly salary between €4.000 and €5.200 (excluding holiday allowance), depending on your experience.</p></li><li><p class="paragraph">an annual on-target bonus of 10% of your gross annual salary;&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="paragraph">full-time employment with 30 days of annual leave;&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="paragraph">a pension scheme;&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="paragraph">a commuting allowance;&nbsp; </p></li><li><p class="paragraph">a dynamic and ambitious working environment where initiative and ownership are valued;</p></li><li><p>the opportunity to grow towards a broader Business Controller role as your knowledge, experience and responsibilities develop;</p></li><li><p class="paragraph">structured coaching by our Data Specialist to develop your data skills alongside your finance role;</p></li><li><p>a friendly, welcoming team, with a free shared lunch every Monday and monthly social drinks.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;"><strong>We are HG</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;">HG is a leading European brand in specialist cleaning and maintenance products.</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;">We believe a home should be a place where people can live carefree, with confidence in the products they use to care for the spaces and belongings around them. Our products are developed to do exactly what they promise: deliver effective, reliable and specialist cleaning solutions that help consumers solve real household problems.</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;">HG’s mission is to help people enjoy their homes without worrying about what might go wrong. We do this through high-quality products, specialist expertise, clear advice and a relentless focus on performance.</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;">We are dedicated to delivering superiority, innovation, quality and customer satisfaction. With a strong presence across Europe and beyond, we are continuously investing to make an even bigger impact.</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;">HG does what it promises.</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;"><strong><br>Do you have any questions?</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;">Our colleague Ilse de Groot, Corporate Recruiter, will be happy to answer any questions. You can contact her at <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;">Would you like to apply for the junior business controller position at HG? You can apply directly by uploading your CV. We aim to respond within 5 working days.</p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><em>Acquisition in response to this vacancy is not appreciated.</em></p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><br></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/hg-international-bv/junior-business-controller-data-specialist-almere-394785","tags":["Finance"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Almere, Flevoland, Nederland","created_at":1795685481},{"slug":"hr-stagiaire-almelo-111104","company_name":"Benchmark","title":"HR-Stagiair(e)","description":"<p class="MsoNormal">Als HR‑Stagiair(e) draai je bij ons mee in het HR‑team en krijg je de kans om veel te leren, met een duidelijke focus op Learning &amp; Development. Je werkt mee aan verschillende HR- en L&amp;D‑activiteiten en krijgt daarnaast de ruimte om je stage zelf vorm te geven en te ontdekken welke andere HR‑onderwerpen jou aanspreken. Zo doe je brede praktijkervaring op in een omgeving waar veel gebeurt en waar je actief kunt bijdragen.</p><p class="MsoNormal"><br><strong>Jouw stage:</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Je werkt mee in ons team van 10 HR‑professionals met expertise in o.a. onboarding, L&amp;D, verzuim, recruitment, employer branding en HR‑advies. Je krijgt veel vrijheid én goede begeleiding om jezelf te ontwikkelen.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Waar draag je aan bij?</strong></p><ul><li><p>Het versterken van vaardigheden en ontwikkeling binnen de organisatie door mee te werken aan L&amp;D‑projecten.</p></li><li><p>Het soepel laten verlopen van soft skills trainingen, door ondersteuning bij voorbereiding, communicatie en coördinatie.</p></li><li><p>De verbetering van HR‑processen door het initiëren en uitvoeren van eigen HR‑projecten (bijvoorbeeld op het gebied van onboarding, recruitment of procesoptimalisatie).</p></li><li><p>Events rondom arbeidsmarktcommunicatie, workshops rond duurzame inzetbaarheid en onboardingsactiviteiten.</p></li><li><p>Een correcte en overzichtelijke HR‑administratie, zoals het opstellen van contracten, brieven en personele mutaties.</p></li><li><p>Continue verbetering binnen HR door actieve deelname aan HR‑overleggen en het meedenken over verbeteringen.</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal">Onze organisatie beweegt snel: er gebeurt veel en geen week is hetzelfde. Dat biedt enorm veel leerkansen, maar vraagt ook dat jij zelf richting geeft aan je stage en je weg vindt in een dynamische omgeving. Je krijgt van ons goede begeleiding, maar het is aan jou om kansen te zien en initiatief te tonen.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Wat breng je mee?</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">We zoeken een stagiair(e) die:</p><ul><li><p>Een hbo‑opleiding HRM volgt (3e of 4e jaar) en stage wil lopen vanaf februari 2027.</p></li><li><p>Beschikbaar is voor 4 of 5 dagen per week.</p></li><li><p>Geïnteresseerd is in Learning &amp; Development.</p></li><li><p>Sterk is in Nederlands en goed overweg kan met Engels.</p></li><li><p>Nauwkeurig werkt, durft te vragen en zelfstandig durft te handelen.</p></li><li><p>Het leuk vindt om in een dynamische omgeving te werken waar veel gebeurt.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Wij bieden:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Stageplek per september 2026 voor 32-40 uur per week.</p></li><li><p>Begeleiding van ervaren HR-professionals.</p></li><li><p>Stagevergoeding van € 650,- per maand op basis van 40 uur.</p></li><li><p>Meedoen met ons Be-Fit programma; wekelijks sporten met collega’s.</p></li><li><p>Ook gewoon een superleuke tijd!</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Over Benchmark</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Benchmark in Almelo maakt onderdeel uit van de multinational Benchmark Electronics Inc., een beursgenoteerde onderneming op het gebied van het vervaardigen van elektronica en het leveren van diensten richting original equipment manufacturers (OEM’s).</p><p class="MsoNormal">Bij Benchmark werk je voor bedrijven die impact maken met hun innovaties. Zo ontwikkelen we nieuwe producten die de veiligheid of gezondheid verbeteren of juist het gemak vergroten. Deze producten worden geleverd vanaf het productontwerp tot en met productie en soms ook rechtstreeks aan de eindgebruiker. Dit gehele proces wordt geheel in Almelo uitgevoerd.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">Wereldwijd heeft Benchmark Electronics Inc. momenteel 23 vestigingen. Op onze vestiging in Almelo werken we samen met zo’n 675 collega’s.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Interesse?</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Benchmark wil vooruit, samen met jou als HR-Stagiair(e)!</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">Ben je op zoek naar meer informatie? Neem dan contact op met Stan Broenink via <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- Ben je geïnteresseerd geraakt in het stagelopen bij een snelgroeiende en internationaal opererende high-tech organisatie? Solliciteer direct!</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">Het verstrekken van een VOG is een vast onderdeel van de sollicitatieprocedure bij Benchmark.</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><em>Acquisitie wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Aan het zonder opdracht, vanuit HR, voorstellen van kandidaten kunnen geen rechten c.q. verplichtingen worden ontleend.</em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/benchmark/hr-stagiaire-almelo-111104","tags":["HR"],"job_types":["Student college","internship"],"location":"Almelo, Overijssel, Nederland","created_at":1795674684},{"slug":"junior-data-consultant-amsterdam-151895","company_name":"LOGEX","title":"Junior Data Consultant","description":"<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;"><strong>Onze Missie</strong></p><p>LOGEX is koploper in data-analyse in de gezondheidzorg. Wij zetten complexe zorgdata om in heldere inzichten waarmee zorgorganisaties grip krijgen op kosten, betere behandelresultaten realiseren en sturen op waardegedreven zorg. Onze oplossingen worden dagelijks gebruikt door meer dan 80 zorginstellingen, zowel publiek als privaat, en maken het verschil in de gezondheidszorg van morgen.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Jouw impact en verantwoordelijkheden</strong></p><ul><li><p>Je verhoogt de kwaliteit van onze dienstverlening door het valideren van financiële en zorginhoudelijke data.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Je communiceert met klanten over hun data-aanlevering en de oplevering van LOGEX modellen.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Je ontwikkelt je in de breedte en biedt ondersteuning aan meerdere teams en klanten als er vragen liggen met betrekking tot de kwaliteit van data.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Je signaleert en realiseert kansen om interne operationele processen te verbeteren.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Je draagt bij aan automatisering van onze operationele processen, mogelijk door inzet van AI.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Team</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Je maakt deel uit van het Financial Analytics Service team, dat momenteel bestaat uit 40 mensen met diverse achtergronden in de gezondheidszorg en data-analyse. Het team is verantwoordelijk voor het implementeren en onderhouden van onze oplossingen en benchmarks, die zowel medische specialisten als de planning- en controleteams in ziekenhuizen ondersteunen. Onze oplossingen helpen ziekenhuizen en medische specialisten bij maandelijkse rapportages over prognoses, het aanpakken van capaciteitsvraagstukken, portefeuillebeslissingen, het verbeteren van patiëntenzorgpaden en andere belangrijke strategische keuzes.&nbsp;</p> <br> <p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Jouw profiel</strong></p><ul><li><p>Relevante werkervaring: Je hebt 0–2 jaar werkervaring en affiniteit met de financiële sector en/of de gezondheidszorg.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Een HBO- of WO-opleiding afgerond, bij voorkeur met een focus op gezondheid, data of economie.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Data-affiniteit: Je hebt interesse in data. Je werkt nauwkeurig, signaleert trends en spoort fouten of afwijkingen op.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Communicatie: Je kunt effectief communiceren met diverse teamleden en interne stakeholders.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Je bent resultaatgericht, werkt gestructureerd en hebt een pragmatische instelling.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Bereidheid om te leren en aan te passen aan innovatieve technologieën, tools en processen.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Een proactieve benadering om nieuwe taken op te pakken en kansen te zoeken om bij te dragen.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Je krijgt energie van het verbeteren van&nbsp; werkprocessen.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Taalvaardigheden: Je spreekt en schrijft vloeiend Nederlands en Engels.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Wat wij bieden:</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Bij LOGEX hebben we één superkracht: data-analyse. Wij kiezen ervoor deze superkracht in te zetten om de huidige problemen in de gezondheidszorg aan te pakken door gegevens te vertalen naar betere zorg.&nbsp;</p><ul><li><p>Een uitstekend beloningspakket (salaris, vakantiegeld, NS Business card, telefoon- en internetvergoeding)&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>25 vakantiedagen (op fulltime basis) om nieuwe energie op te doen, met de mogelijkheid om extra vakantiedagen te kopen&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Een informele werkomgeving met gedreven collega’s&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>De mogelijkheid tot hybride werken&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Een laptop en alles wat je nodig hebt om thuis een comfortabele en ergonomische werkplek in te richten&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Persoonlijke en professionele ontwikkeling via onze LOGEX Academy&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Toegang tot onze partner op het gebied van mentale gezondheid; OpenUp&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Regelmatig borrels na het werk en nog veel meer evenementen&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>€240 jaarlijkse health benefit</p></li><li><p>Mogelijkheid om een elektrische fiets te leasen via het fietsplan.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;"><strong>Klaar om mee te bouwen aan de toekomst van de zorg?</strong></p><p style="text-align:start;">Je kunt solliciteren via onderstaande knop en je CV uploaden. Voor meer informatie, of als je vragen hebt, kun je contact opnemen met Wesley Schreuder op <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Ons bedrijf zet zich in voor het creëren van een werkplek die gelijkheid, diversiteit en inclusie bevordert. Wij geloven dat een diverse workforce essentieel is voor ons succes. Terwijl we blijven streven naar een werkomgeving waarin iedereen zich gewaardeerd en gerespecteerd voelt – ongeacht ras, gender, seksuele geaardheid, leeftijd, religie of andere kenmerken – moedigen wij iedereen aan om te solliciteren.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/logex/junior-data-consultant-amsterdam-151895","tags":[],"job_types":["Entry","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1795674683},{"slug":"android-engineer-amsterdam-442072","company_name":"Aquablu B.V","title":"Android Engineer","description":"<h2>Who are we?</h2><p>We're a smart hydration company rebuilding an industry that still runs on sugar water and single-use packaging.<br>Filtered water, functional flavors, zero bottles. Still, sparkling, cold, and hot. All poured from one tap. We create hydration people want to reach for, starting with the workplace where we help teams thrive.<br><br>As an AI-native company, we build at speed. In 2025, Aquablu ranked 2nd in the Deloitte Technology Fast 50 (Netherlands) and 30th in the Sifted 250 (Europe), both rankings of the fastest-growing companies by revenue growth. In 2026 we were named a winner of Maya's Culture 100 Europe Awards as one of the best workplaces to thrive in.<br><br>Growing that fast and thriving comes down to our people. Our team is our biggest asset and one that we’re proud of. We’re committed to maintaining our vibrant culture as we continue to grow.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2>About the role</h2><p>Aquablu's products run Android in more places than your pocket. Our dispensing systems ship with Android-powered on-device software that hundreds of thousands of people touch every day, and our mobile apps put hydration in users' hands. As our Android Engineer, you work across that whole surface.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Your main arena is on-device: the software running on the hardware itself, where Android meets the physical world. Screens people tap on a machine, software that talks to firmware, updates that roll out to hundreds of deployed systems in the field. Alongside that, you contribute to our mobile development where the products need it. Few Android roles give you this range.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>This is a hands-on engineering role in a small, fast team. You own features end to end and deliver them reliably, reaching out to your manager when support is needed to unblock you. You build with AI agents as your default collaborator, you work cross-functionally with hardware, firmware, and product, proactively identifying and reaching out to key players that can help filling any gaps. </p><p>This role reports into our Head of Digital Product, and is part of Aquablu’s Software &amp; Intelligence Engineering team.</p> <br> <h2>What You'll Build &amp; Own</h2><ul><li><p><strong>On-device Android software:</strong> Features on the user-facing software running on our dispensing systems — UI, device behaviour, and the integration layer where software meets hardware. You own your features end to end.</p></li><li><p><strong>Fleet-ready releases:</strong> Contribute to releases that update reliably across hundreds of deployed devices in the field, where a broken release means a technician visit. The riskiest releases get a second pair of senior eyes — and you learn what makes them safe.</p></li><li><p><strong>Hardware &amp; firmware integration:</strong> Work with embedded and firmware engineers to define and implement serial APIs (UART), that expose device state and trigger mechanical actions.</p></li><li><p><strong>Mobile contribution:</strong> Support Android development on our consumer app where the roadmap needs it.</p></li><li><p><strong>AI-native development:</strong> Build with AI agents every day and keep pushing what that lets you ship.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2>What You Bring</h2><ul><li><p>Solid Android engineering experience: A minimum of 3-5 years building and shipping Android apps in Kotlin, with a solid grasp of the platform (lifecycle, concurrency). You should be able to judge which Android patterns fit a non-standard system, and to design features that contribute to a scalable, reliable system. </p></li><li><p>Curiosity for Android beyond the traditional mobile world: kiosk, embedded, or AOSP work is a strong plus. Pragmatic problem solver who’s comfortable working outside of familiar mobile patterns.</p></li><li><p>Work independently on well-scoped tasks. When scope is unclear, flag it, reach out to the right people, and get the answers and support you need to unblock yourself. Plan the work, communicate progress early, and deliver end to end.</p></li><li><p>AI-native coding is how you work. You build with AI agents daily, you have a sharp setup, and your output shows it. If your last six months of work doesn't look meaningfully different because of AI, this isn't your role.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2 style="text-align:start;"><strong>✨ Why join us?</strong></h2><ul><li><p><strong>💰 A salary between 66-89k yearly (incl. 8% holiday allowance)</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>📈 Equity through our Aquablu for All plan: it's not just about shares, it's about shared success.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>🏋️ Urban Sports Club Membership</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>🌱 Healthy (heavily discounted) lunches</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>🎯 Purpose with Impact: shape how the world hydrates while wiping out single-use plastics.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>📋 Scale-up pace means fresh challenges (and new skills) every quarter.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>🤝 Join an ambitious, bold, and fun crew that's always got your back.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>🌱 Company-sponsored gym membership keeps mind and body in sync.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>💰 Pension plan with Zwitserleven (50/50 split) so you grow while your savings do, too.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>🎵 What kind of vibe can you expect at our office? Check out our very own Spotify playlist "<a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://open.spotify.com/playlist/5ZFg45ef7TFEMH2uhclCK8?si=959691b0b95a48d2&nd=1&dlsi=d74dc5649b6c4038">Akwablues</a>"</strong></p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>🎬 Curious about our story &amp; culture? Check our documentaries on <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.youtube.com/@aquabluofficial/videos">Youtube</a>!</strong></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/aquablu-bv/android-engineer-amsterdam-442072","tags":["Product & Engineering"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1795674680},{"slug":"account-executive-the-hague-341624","company_name":"Eye Security","title":"Account Executive (m/f/x)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Eye</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Eye Security provides cybersecurity and embedded cyber insurance solutions for organizations across Europe. Headquartered in the Netherlands, we’ve grown to over 170 employees and continue to expand internationally.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We combine cutting-edge technology with hands-on expertise to detect, respond to, and recover from cyber threats in real time. Our team unites professionals from intelligence, military, tech, and consulting backgrounds - all driven by one mission: to make enterprise-grade cybersecurity accessible to every business, not just the big players.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Role at Eye</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will own and manage full sales cycle from discovery to closing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will act as the primary point of contact for assigned partners (broker and MSP), ensuring strong engagement, enablement, and deal progression.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will build and maintain pipeline mainly through partner engagement and follow-up on marketing and partner leads.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will apply solution selling principles: identify customer pain points, sell the value of minimizing risk, and articulate why Eye’s solutions are worth the investment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will recognize opportunities for market growth within your assigned region and partner ecosystem.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will collaborate with Product and Marketing teams and represent Eye at industry events.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have experience in a commercial development role, within SaaS environment and a solid foundation in customer discovery, qualification, and value-based conversations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are eager to learn about selling IT infrastructure solutions or managed services and understand how value can be created through reliability, risk reduction, and business continuity, not just cost.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You demonstrate good interpersonal skills and are comfortable building relationships with customers and internal or external partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have an interest in structured sales methodologies (e.g. MEDDPICC or similar) and are motivated to apply them in practice.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are proactive, motivated, and take ownership of your work, with a strong willingness to learn and grow in a sales role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are fluent in English and Dutch (spoken and written) and willing to travel up to 20% of the time.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will become part of one of the fastest growing cybersecurity scale-ups in Europe.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will play a key role in building an innovative cybersecurity product line where we combine effective cybersecurity with cyber insurance on a global scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An attractive remuneration package and bonus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Car allowance and “floating holidays” for additional time off.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">MacBook or Windows Laptop and iPhone or Samsung company phone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong support for your personal and professional development.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regular company-wide get-togethers, giving you the opportunity to collaborate in person and build strong team connections.</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/eye-security/account-executive-the-hague-341624","tags":["Business"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"The Hague - hybrid","created_at":1795664588},{"slug":"senior-data-engineer-amsterdam-area-421741","company_name":"Everfield","title":"Senior Data Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Everfield: Senior Data Engineer</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Company</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everfield is a platform with a mission in acquiring, building, and operating vertical market and specialist software companies, focused on European businesses. We invest in and provide support and best practices to software companies in order for them to live up to their full potential by offering a very established approach to promote growth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everfield is looking to be the leader in European Vertical and specialist software solutions across myriad niche industries who provide mission-critical applications, service, and support to their clients.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everfield seeks to deliver innovation and growth to its acquired companies by providing best practices and operational support to help identify opportunities and install proven methodologies to accelerate customer and market share. Everfield is located throughout Europe, with offices in the UK, Germany, the Netherlands, France, Poland, Spain, and Latvia.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Position</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Senior Data Engineer at Everfield, you will leverage your expertise and experience to:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continuously improve scalability and stability of our data platform called the <em>Lakehouse</em></p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create new data pipeline solutions on various data sources (ERP, CRMs, etc.)</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and model data in a common data model and Kimball-style dimensional models, making it ready for consumption in Power BI and other tools</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Further developing <em>Lakehouse Lumen</em>, our MCP server that makes Lakehouse data available to Claude for end users</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve existing solutions to improve value add for various stakeholders</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll be working as part of the Business Intelligence (BI) team. Currently the team consists of a Lead Data Engineer, three Data Analysts and a hands-on team lead. The BI team creates value for various stakeholders (CEO, Finance, COO, Sales, Marketing, and Everfield’sportfolio companies), by creating insights, delivering analysis, automating reporting processes and improving data quality.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The team builds pipelines with <strong>Azure Databricks</strong> and <strong>Azure Synapse Analytics </strong>to ingest the data into our data platform, uses <strong>Azure Databricks</strong> for data transformation, <strong>Power BI</strong> for data visualization and <strong>Azure Container Apps</strong> to expose data via a MCP server to Claude. For most solutions, the team uses <strong>Python</strong> and <strong>SQL</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For many use cases we work in an agentic way, using Claude to plan and implement them. To support this, we built the "Lakehouse DevKit". A set of agents and skills that we plan to keep extending and improving.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is hybrid from Amsterdam area.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Adhere to the DevOps methodology by:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with the Lead Data Engineer and Team Lead to plan and prioritize tasks.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop data pipelines in Azure Databricks and Azure Synapse Analytics, along with data ingestion and process scripts using PySpark and Pandas, while managing version control through Git.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve and extend the MCP server that provides data to Claude.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create unit tests, test your own work and review work of colleagues (via Pull Requests), to ensure quality control.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Extend the Lakehouse DevKit to support and accelerate agentic development workflows.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enhance and maintain deployment pipelines to facilitate smooth releases to end users.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor the data platform (including data pipelines, ingestion/processing jobs, and alerts), while continuously improving logging and monitoring practices.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ideal Candidate Profile</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hard Skills</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Required:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ year of experience as <strong>Data Engineer</strong>, and 5+ years of professional experience within Data or related fields.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expert in <strong>PySpark</strong> and <strong>Pandas</strong> for data processing.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with <strong>Databricks</strong> for advanced analytics.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong knowledge of <strong>SQL</strong> and <strong>data modeling</strong> (especially star schema).</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with <strong>financial systems</strong> (ERP, NetSuite, SAP) and/or experience with <strong>CRM</strong> systems and <strong>customer</strong> <strong>data</strong>.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nice to have:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with Claude Code (agents, skills)</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of <strong>Power Query</strong> and <strong>Power BI</strong> for data visualization.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience deploying Azure resources like <strong>Azure Container Apps</strong>.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Soft Skills</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Independent Worker</strong>: Ability to operate autonomously while contributing effectively to team goals.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Business Acumen</strong>: Strong understanding of business and economic principles, with an ability to apply them in a data context.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Analytical Mindset</strong>: Excellent problem-solving and critical thinking skills.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaborative</strong>: Actively seeks alignment with team members and participates in planning sessions.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Quality-Focused</strong>: Committed to reviewing both your own work and that of others to maintain high standards.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strategic Planner</strong>: Consider alternative solutions and refine features before implementation.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Purpose-Driven</strong>: Demonstrates a deep understanding of tasks, ensuring they align with business objectives.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What’s in it for you?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Grow your career in a fast-paced and growing organization.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enable growth by building a robust and scalable data platform.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working with the latest Data Engineering &amp; Data Modeling technologies.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Long term career opportunities.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working from home for up to 4 days per week.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible work environment with offices around Europe (Netherlands, UK, Spain, France, Poland, Germany).</p></